<!-- event-labels: generated by tools/build-mod.py from cards/trees/*.tree.json.
     Do not hand-edit. Appended to vanilla text_events.xml; last definition wins. -->

<text name="text_EMPTY_STATION2_TEXT_1">[ Abandoned station ]

You find a small space station that appears to be abandoned.</text>

<text name="text_EMPTY_STATION2_TEXT_2">[ Abandoned station ]

You arrive to find what appears to be a colonized moon, however scans show it has been abandoned. You also detect an abandoned space station near the Beacon.</text>

<text name="text_EMPTY_STATION2_TEXT_3">[ Abandoned station ]

This area shows signs of a battle some time ago. There are scattered remains of ships but one station appears to be intact.</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_CRYSTAL_BEACON_text">[ Ancient device ]

An ancient device is orbiting within the crystal rings of a nearby gas giant. You can't discern its nature or function, but it seems to have been deactivated for a very long time. Perhaps you can get some scrap from it.</text>

<text name="event_CIVILIAN_ASTEROIDS_BEACON_text">[ Asteroid belt distress ]

You follow the distress beacon to a tiny asteroid belt. You find a small ship struggling to maneuver through the field.</text>

<text name="event_HELP_MINERS_text">[ Asteroid mining colony ]

You come across an asteroid mining colony. They message you immediately, saying, "Greetings. Our supplies of mining explosives have run out ever since the Rebels blockaded this system. Do you have any extra explosives?"</text>

<text name="event_AUTO_CIVILIAN_text">[ Auto-ship attacking civilian ]

You come across a Rebel automated scout ship pursuing a civilian ship, weapons engaged.</text>

<text name="event_AUTO_REFUEL_STATION_text">[ Auto-ship attacking outpost ]

You detect an automated Rebel scout attacking a small refueling outpost.</text>

<text name="event_AUTO_HACKER_text">[ Auto-ship carrying shield virus ]

Your arrival is greeted by numerous computer alerts. The nearby automated Rebel scout has used a local satellite to deploy a virus to disrupt your Shields System. Hopefully it won't cause further problems before you can destroy it.</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_AUTO_text">[ Auto-ship fight (Crystal) ]

The Rebels must have sent their automated scouts to find you. One jumps in and immediately moves to attack.</text>

<text name="event_AUTO_ASTEROID_text">[ Auto-ship fight in asteroid field ]

You arrive in an asteroid belt to discover that a Rebel automated-scout has been stationed here. Prepare for a fight!</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_AUTO_LIST_1">[ Auto-ship fight in nebula ]

You cross paths with an advance scout of the Rebel fleet searching this section of the nebula for your ship.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_AUTO_LIST_2">[ Auto-ship fight in nebula ]

You jump into a calmer part of the nebula. However, your relief fades as a Rebel scout jumps to the beacon and moves in to attack.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_AUTO_LIST_3">[ Auto-ship fight in nebula ]

The tangled wrecks of many ships wait in dormancy here. You see lights flicker on what looks like debris. A Rebel scout bursts out of the wreckage!</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_AUTO_LIST_4">[ Auto-ship fight in nebula ]

This drone isn't looking for you. Perhaps it's scouting ahead for the Rebel expansion or maybe they're seeking to use this nebula for cover. Regardless, it identifies you as hostile.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_AUTO_LIST_5">[ Auto-ship fight in nebula ]

It's worrying that the Rebels have penetrated so deep into uncharted space, even if it is only an unmanned craft. It arms its weapons; you should do the same.</text>

<text name="event_STORM_AUTO_text">[ Auto-ship fight in plasma storm ]

You jump into a sector of the nebula beset by a plasma storm. An automated Rebel scout stationed at the beacon moves in to attack.</text>

<text name="event_AUTO_SUN_text">[ Auto-ship fight near sun ]

You arrive at the beacon to find yourself dangerously close to a star. An automated Rebel ship, impervious to the heat, moves in to engage.</text>

<text name="event_AUTO_DEFENSE_RADAR_text">[ Auto-ship near radar station ]

A Rebel automated ship sits dormant near a Rebel forward radar station.</text>

<text name="event_AUTO_DEFENSE_MAP_text">[ Auto-ship near sensor station ]

You detect a Rebel automated ship nearby. It does not engage and seems to be patrolling around a long-range sensor station.</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_AUTO_DEFENSE_ITEM_text">[ Auto-ship near storage station in nebula ]

An advance Rebel automated ship remains stationed near a small Rebel space-station. However, without functioning sensors it is impossible to tell what is inside.</text>

<text name="event_AUTO_DEFENSE_ITEM_text">[ Auto-ship near storage station ]

An advanced Rebel automated ship remains stationed near a small Rebel space-station. Sensors indicate it's a storage vessel for military goods.</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_AUTO_WARNING_text">[ Auto-ship warning in nebula ]

It appears that an automated Rebel scout was positioned within the nebula to warn of your passing.</text>

<text name="event_BATTLEFIELD_SURVIVOR_text">[ Battlefield survivor ]

Your bring the survivor aboard, but discover their wounds are severe. They won't live much longer.</text>

<text name="text_WRECKAGE_TEXT_1">[ Battlefield wreckage ]

What at first seems to be a simple nebula is actually filled with a good amount of debris from a brutal exchange between several ships. Wreckage drifts by your screens and tumbles into the depths of the nebula to be lost to sight. It's hard to determine who the combatants were without closer investigation.</text>

<text name="text_WRECKAGE_TEXT_2">[ Battlefield wreckage ]

You have jumped into the aftermath of what seems to have been a brutal exchange between several ships. Wreckage drifts by your screens, and you can still see the remains of the dying ships sparking and breaking apart. It's hard to determine who the combatants were without closer investigation.</text>

<text name="event_BOARDERS_ASTEROID_GHOST_text">[ Boarders: Ghosts in a ship graveyard ]

You jump into the middle of an asteroid field. Looking around, you find you are surrounded by dozens of wrecks of other ships. Faint wisps of light can be seen moving between wrecks. As you watch, they seem to be changing path and floating toward your ship!</text>

<text name="event_BOARDERS_ASTEROID_text">[ Boarders in asteroid field ]

You jump into a perilous asteroid field. Worse, sensors show a pirate stronghold has locked onto our ship and is activating a teleporter. Prepare for a fight!</text>

<text name="text_BOARDERS_CRYSTAL_1">[ Boarders: Crystal ]

You detect a heavily armed Crystalline ship escorting some sort of prison vessel. Scans indicate there are a number of non-Crystal based life forms aboard; they must be rounding up all of the intruders in their space! Before you can react, you hear the telltale sounds of a teleporter going off.</text>

<text name="text_BOARDERS_CRYSTAL_2">[ Boarders: Crystal ]

You arrive near a small settlement and a lone guard ship moves to intercept you. You try to contact them but they are refusing all hails. Suddenly you hear lasers ricocheting from within the ship. You've been boarded!</text>

<text name="text_BOARDERS_CRYSTAL_3">[ Boarders: Crystal ]

You pick up chatter from a nearby ship, "Yes... Here are some interesting specimens. Try to take them alive this time, there's a lot of money to be had on aliens." Scanners indicate a remote teleporter was just used.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_PIRATE_BOARDERS_text">[ Boarders: Humans (Abandoned) ]

An image of some weak and hungry humans comes onto your screen. "Those metal bastards think they can just absorb half of our engines and leave us here to die? I hope you understand the need to take your ship by force."</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_BOARDING_TEXT_1">[ Boarders: Humans in nebula ]

You see a small station nearby and feel the shudder of shots ringing through the ship. You can't be sure without sensors, but it seems there may be intruders on the ship!</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_BOARDING_TEXT_2">[ Boarders: Humans in nebula ]

You arrive in the nebula and immediately receive a message from an unknown source, "Prepare to be boarded!" With the static from the nebula, there's no way to tell where they came from, but you hear shots fired on board the ship.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_BOARDING_TEXT_3">[ Boarders: Humans in nebula ]

You see a number of derelict ships near this beacon. After a short time you hear the tell-tale sounds of a teleporter and shouts coming from within the ship. You've been boarded!</text>

<text name="event_STORM_BOARDING_text">[ Boarders: Humans in plasma storm ]

You find two heavily damaged ships floating nearby, the remains of a battle. You begin to harvest some usable debris when you hear the sounds of someone beaming aboard followed by the shouts of a boarding party.</text>

<text name="event_BOARDERS_HACKING_text">[ Boarders: Humans jammed sensors ]

You catch a glimpse of a strange signal coming from a space station before your sensors shut off unexpectedly. As you discover that your sensors are being jammed, you hear hostiles beam onto your ship.</text>

<text name="event_BOARDERS_SUN_text">[ Boarders: Humans near sun ]

You arrive to find yourself extremely close to a star. You receive a message from a pirate ship, "I'm glad you arrived; our ship is damaged and we were getting desperate... I hope you don't mind if we take yours." Hostiles detected on board our ship!</text>

<text name="text_BOARDERS_TEXT_1">[ Boarders: Humans (Pirate) ]

What appears to be a civilian ship sends a friendly hail. As you approach the vessel, you detect a teleporter signal but it's too late... intruders have beamed aboard!</text>

<text name="text_BOARDERS_TEXT_2">[ Boarders: Humans (Pirate) ]

A heavily damaged ship is drifting near this beacon. You receive a communication: "Hello! Nice of you to drop by. As you can see, our ship has seen better days. Yours is looking quite nice, I think we might be taking it from you now." Intruders beam aboard.</text>

<text name="text_BOARDERS_TEXT_3">[ Boarders: Humans (Pirate) ]

You detect life-signs actually on the beacon itself! A teleporter signal warns you but it's too late, they've beamed from the beacon onto your ship and seem intent on taking it over.</text>

<text name="text_BOARDERS_TEXT_4">[ Boarders: Humans (Pirate) ]

Your ship detects a faint distress signal on a nearby moon. As you approach the rock, warning lights flash as hostiles beam aboard the ship from some hidden location.</text>

<text name="text_BOARDERS_TEXT_5">[ Boarders: Humans (Pirate) ]

As you arrive, you become aware of a small Rebel outpost near the beacon. You are hardly able to bark an order before a small team is beamed aboard your ship. They must have been expecting you...</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_BOARDERS_1">[ Boarders: Mantis ]

A derelict and still smoking Mantis vessel floats by. The battle must have been recent; its surviving crew beam aboard. Prepare for a fight!</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_BOARDERS_2">[ Boarders: Mantis ]

Your world, all of a sudden, changes. The Mantis are on board your ship.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_BOARDERS_3">[ Boarders: Mantis ]

You hear a grating rattle and a soft clicking. You reach for your pistol.</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_REBEL_BOARDING_text">[ Boarders: rebels in nebula ]

There appear to be a number of small stations nearby. Before you have time to scan them, warnings go off. A Rebel teleporter was used in one of the stations. You've been boarded!</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_BOARDERS_SUN_1">[ Boarders: Rockmen near sun ]

As soon as you arrive you hear the telltale sounds of a teleporter and shouts reverberating through the ship, "Prepare to burn, fleshy meat-sack aliens!"</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_BOARDERS_SUN_2">[ Boarders: Rockmen near sun ]

With their high resistance to heat, outlaw Rocks often settle very close to stars. That is why it is hardly surprising when your ship gets boarded as you stumble past a hidden settlement.</text>

<text name="event_BOSS_AUTOMATED_text">[ Flagship goes automated ]

It appears this ship is also equipped with an advanced AI system. Now that the crew is dead, it has taken control!</text>

<text name="event_BOSS_DESTROYED_text">[ Flagship destroyed ]

Its explosion rocks your ship and you shudder with relief. You did it. The Federation is saved....</text>

<text name="event_BOSS_ESCAPED_text">[ Flagship escapes a phase ]

Just as you finally gain the upper hand it finds a way to make an FTL jump. You've got to keep up the assault!</text>

<text name="event_BOSS_STALEMATE_text">[ Stalemate - the ship jumps away ]

The ship jumped away without warning. You prepare to pursue.</text>

<text name="event_BOSS_TEXT_1_text">[ Rebel Flagship, phase 1 ]

This is it... The Rebel flagship. If you are able to destroy this monstrosity, the Federation fleet will have a chance of surviving. There's no turning back!</text>

<text name="event_BOSS_TEXT_2_text">[ Rebel Flagship, phase 2 ]

You chase down the flagship and discover it is heavily damaged from the previous fight. Scans indicate that it has redirected considerable power to its drones. Get ready for a fight.</text>

<text name="event_BOSS_TEXT_3_text">[ Rebel Flagship, phase 3 ]

You're not certain how it's able to keep fighting with the amount of damage it has sustained. It looks like it's transferred power to the teleporter as well as... some kind of super weapon. Be prepared... this is it!</text>

<text name="event_QUEST_CREWDEAD_START_text">[ Capture the ship ]

You arrive to find a number of ships convening around a station. There is some unencrypted chatter between the ships, you tune in and listen for anything interesting.</text>

<text name="event_CIVILIAN_ASTEROIDS_BEACON_2_text">[ Civilian asteroids beacon 2 ]

They respond: "Help! Our shields are down and we won't last long!"</text>

<text name="event_CONFUSED_MANTIS_text">[ Confused Mantis ]

As soon as you jump into the system, you receive a hail from a nearby civilian Engi vessel. Their Captain appears on your screen: "Strange bug. Can you assist in debugging?"</text>

<text name="text_TAVERN_HIRE_TEXT_1">[ Crew hiring station ]

You find a space station set up for travelers. Browsing through its listings, you find a tavern full of mercenaries for hire. You look for potential crewmembers.</text>

<text name="text_TAVERN_HIRE_TEXT_2">[ Crew hiring station ]

There are a number of ships stationed around a rest stop. You immediately receive a message saying, "If you're looking for some bodies to fill your ship, you've come to the right place!"</text>

<text name="text_TAVERN_HIRE_TEXT_3">[ Crew hiring station ]

This Beacon seems to serve as a meeting place for local traffic. It seems you can find crew willing to fight on your ship here... for a price.</text>

<text name="event_CREW_STUCK_text">[ Crew stranded - teleporter destroyed ]

With your teleporter damaged and no way to fix it, you take one of the enemy ship's shuttles to return to your own ship.</text>

<text name="event_DISTRESS_TRAPPED_MINER_text">[ Crushed pirate ]

You arrive at the distress beacon near a small asteroid belt and find a ship with pirate markings partially crushed between two large rocks. It must have been illegally mining the belt without proper equipment.</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_CHATTY_text">[ Crystal chat ]

A small civilian vessel messages you, "Wow! You're that alien that opened up the portal, aren't you! Are you busy? Can I ask you a question?"</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_REBEL_CRYSTAL2_text">[ Crystal fight choice ]

You're greeted by an unwelcome sight - a Rebel advance ship is laying down fire on a Crystalline vessel in the distance.</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_CONVOY_text">[ Crystal fight with surrender offer (hull repairs) ]

A large convoy of lumbering civilian ships appears to be passing through this region. You show no hostile intentions, but they are taking no chances, immediately sending their escort to attack!</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_HUNTER_text">[ Crystal fight with surrender offer (Human crew) ]

Crystal shards fly past your ship as soon as you jump. You scan to find the assailant and discover a Crystalline ship carrying a number of humans in its cargo bay. It must be hunting the intruding ships!</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_SCRAP_EXCITED_text">[ Crystal scrap collector ]

You receive a signal from a private relay on a nearby inhabited planet. "Are you the alien ship they've been talking about?! You are! Please, I am a collector of alien artifacts, I'm sure what is scrap to you is priceless to me."</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_FED_text">[ Crystal ship attacking Federation loyalists ]

There appears to be a fight going on nearby. A Crystalline border guard is chasing a small Federation ship!</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_UNLOCK_text">[ Crystal unlock ]

You arrive at the coordinates to find a massive Crystalline cruiser docked at a small repair station. You arrange for the ship to be sent back to the Federation base while the station upgrades your hull.</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_CACHE_text">[ Crystalline cache ]

Odd radar pings from a huge, orbiting asteroid here reveal a Crystalline cache of some kind. A deep crater has been sealed over with a thick layer of crystal to keep whatever's inside safe - it'd take some serious firepower to break though.</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_HELP_DIG_text">[ Crystalline men buried ]

A large Crystalline ship is floating in space here. They hail: "Aliens?! How curious. We request your aid. We have men buried on a nearby planet and we must dig them out."</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_HUMAN_TESTS_text">[ Crystalline research facility ]

You arrive near what appears to be a Crystalline research facility. A scientist quickly messages you, "Ah! You're those aliens! Please, I've heard so much about you and I'm really curious about your physiology! Would you let us run a few simple tests?"</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_REQUEST_text">[ Crystalline ship messaging about Rebels ]

The moment you arrive you notice a Crystalline ship in the vicinity keeping its distance. They message you, "The 'Rebels' that are trying to hunt YOU down are creating havoc everywhere they go."</text>

<text name="event_BROKEN_REBEL_DRONE_text">[ Deactivated Auto-ship ]

You find a Rebel automated scout floating near this beacon. Despite its pristine condition, it appears to be de-activated.</text>

<text name="event_ASTEROID_DERELICT_SHIP_text">[ Dense asteroid field distress ]

A ship without life forms within a nearby dense asteroid field is giving off the distress call. Shall we investigate? It could be dangerous.</text>

<text name="event_FLOATING_CARGO_text">[ Destroyed cargo ship ]

Not too far from the beacon, you detect a destroyed cargo ship with its cargo scattered nearby, intact.</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_LOOTING_text">[ Disabled Rock ship ]

You find a disabled rock transport floating near the beacon. You consider stripping it of useful parts but are uncertain why it's there in the first place.</text>

<text name="event_DISTRESS_ENGI_REBEL_RESULT_text">[ Distress Engi Rebel result ]

The Engi vessel turns out to be very poorly equipped - barely a runabout, really. They're trying to outrun the Rebels, and need all the help they can get.</text>

<text name="event_DOCK_BOMB_SALESMAN_text">[ Pirate bomb salesman ]

A human in an exquisite suit meets you on board. "Welcome to my ship! We specialize in explosives of all kinds, can I interest you in any?"</text>

<text name="event_DOCK_DRONE_SALESMAN_text">[ Pirate drone salesman ]

A human in an exquisite suit meets you on board. "Welcome to my ship! We specialize in drones of all kinds, can I interest you in any?"</text>

<text name="event_DONOR_MANTIS_CHASE2_text">[ Mantis ship-collectors, rematch ]

You catch up with the Mantis ship that escaped before, only to see them transferring their crew into an even bigger ship!</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_1">[ Empty beacon (Civilian) ]

Your jump leads you to nothing but empty space. This Jump Beacon serves no purpose other than as a connection.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_2">[ Empty beacon (Civilian) ]

You jump into an unremarkable system. No life signs detected within scanning range.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_3">[ Empty beacon (Civilian) ]

Your scans reveal a mining base on a nearby planet long since abandoned. No life signs detected.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_4">[ Empty beacon (Civilian) ]

Your scans reveal an ore refinery and several factories, all standing still and empty. No life signs detected.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_5">[ Empty beacon (Civilian) ]

You discover a nearby planet speckled with settlements, although none respond to your hails.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_6">[ Empty beacon (Civilian) ]

This beacon has been built for a nearby civilian space-station. No one hails your ship.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_7">[ Empty beacon (Civilian) ]

The nearby planet shows sign of habitation and great beauty. A rudimentary automated planetary defense system is looping its message into space: "Warning! Quarantine Level 5 in effect under FHA Act 22, article 11.2. Warning! Quarantine Level 5..."</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_8">[ Empty beacon (Civilian) ]

Your jump leads to a completely unremarkable binary star system. There is nothing else around.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_9">[ Empty beacon (Civilian) ]

Your jump leads to a remarkable binary star system. The view is beautiful, but there is nothing else around.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ENGI_1">[ Empty beacon (Engi) ]

The complex arrangements of ship hulls and FTL drive capacitors floating abandoned in space suggest the Engi were here not too long ago; but no longer.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ENGI_2">[ Empty beacon (Engi) ]

You arrive at a green planet with great plains and rolling waterfalls. It would be of little interest to the Engi nearby.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ENGI_3">[ Empty beacon (Engi) ]

You have arrived near an Engi construction yard. Most Engi maintain their bi-pedal appearance out of habit but here you see a number of Engi hives working together to create massive organic machines adept at building ships. Truly a sight to behold.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ENGI_4">[ Empty beacon (Engi) ]

Even though each "individual" Engi is made up of trillions of nano-machines, their culture still revolves around traditional social interactions. A nearby station seems to be constructed for entertainment of passing Engi travellers.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ENGI_5">[ Empty beacon (Engi) ]

You see a number of Engi space stations and fleets nearby. Despite looking like piles of junk loosely tied together they are actually a model of efficiency. They just lack a certain aesthetic emphasis in their constructions.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ENGI_6">[ Empty beacon (Engi) ]

This system appears quite peaceful. You're not sure how long it'll last between the combined threats of the Rebels and Mantis.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ENGI_7">[ Empty beacon (Engi) ]

There are a number of merchant ships passing through the area despite the threat of Mantis invasion. No doubt interested in buying the efficient technology of the Engi.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ENGI_8">[ Empty beacon (Engi) ]

You see a small Rebel carrier in the distance. You lay low and try to blend in with the other traffic. However it's surprising to see a Rebel military ship alone deep in Engi space.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ENGI_9">[ Empty beacon (Engi) ]

The Engi seem to have avoided this particular node, along with every other life-form. You keep your eyes peeled for reasons why, but spin up the FTL without event.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ENGI_10">[ Empty beacon (Engi) ]

A cluster of Engi satellites in orbit of a nearby planet are the only clue the mechanical species was ever here. You have other places to be.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_MANTIS_1">[ Empty beacon (Mantis) ]

At this point you almost expect a fight with the Mantis, but this beacon appears to be entirely devoid of other ships. You take the time to catch your breath and double check the ship's systems.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_MANTIS_2">[ Empty beacon (Mantis) ]

The only thing this beacon offers is a view of deep space and a brief respite from battles. For some this must be a welcome refuge.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_MANTIS_3">[ Empty beacon (Mantis) ]

A nearby Mantis mining operation is clearly using heavy Engi slave labor. You briefly consider the possibility of emancipating the slaves, but the Mantis presence is too formidable. You decide to lay low.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_MANTIS_4">[ Empty beacon (Mantis) ]

There aren't so many parts of Mantis space that aren't dotted by the wrecks of battles past, but this is one of them. You take a deep breath and prepare to move on.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_MANTIS_5">[ Empty beacon (Mantis) ]

There's nothing here but space debris and some uninhabitable planetoids.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_MANTIS_6">[ Empty beacon (Mantis) ]

You fancy you see something moving in the shadow of the beacon, but all remains still.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_PIRATE_1">[ Empty beacon (Pirate) ]

As soon as you arrive, a small ship de-cloaks behind yours. You immediately power up the shields and weapons, but they continue on their trajectory unimpressed. You try to calm your nerves.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_PIRATE_2">[ Empty beacon (Pirate) ]

A small pirate ship messages you, "That sure is a shiny ship you got there." You fire a warning shot across their bow and they respond, "Hey! No need for violence! It was just a comment..."</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_PIRATE_3">[ Empty beacon (Pirate) ]

The only thing within scanning range is an old abandoned mining structure and a resupply station. They appear to have been picked clean by marauders.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_PIRATE_4">[ Empty beacon (Pirate) ]

You arrive to have a small fleet of Engi ships target you with a message, "Piracy results in negative societal impact. Not permitted." You assure them of your honest intentions and they allow you to pass.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_REBEL_1">[ Empty beacon (Rebel) ]

You enter a system bustling with Rebel activity. Supply freighters and re-supply stations are dwarfed by a few heavy warships. Luckily, no one seems to be paying attention to small cruisers. No ships are scanning or messaging you.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_REBEL_2">[ Empty beacon (Rebel) ]

You arrive near a small Rebel refueling depot. Your ship is being scanned multiple times so they must recognize you, but there appears to be no combat-ready ships in the vicinity. The only message you receive is a denial to your request to dock at the depot.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_REBEL_3">[ Empty beacon (Rebel) ]

There is not much of interest nearby. A small sun in the distance with a few orbiting planets in nearby space provide little of interest.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_REBEL_4">[ Empty beacon (Rebel) ]

There are no other ships near this beacon, however you detect a small communication relay. You tap into it without a problem; there is no encryption. Most of the chatter revolves around troop and fleet movements, not particularly interesting.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_REBEL_5">[ Empty beacon (Rebel) ]

There is a small planet nearby with scattered settlements. A small Rebel fleet is in orbit with many ships ferrying back and forth. It must be a more recently 'liberated' planet.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ROCK_1">[ Empty beacon (Rock) ]

You receive a message meant to degrade you as aliens. You half expect an attack but it seems to have come from a small civilian shuttle.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ROCK_2">[ Empty beacon (Rock) ]

No one bothers your ship as you float among numerous space stations and mining platforms. The Rock certainly run efficient operations.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ROCK_3">[ Empty beacon (Rock) ]

You arrive and detect signs of battle. A few ships are taking passes at each other near a small station. You don't know if it's a territory issue, a contest or a rite of passage but you decide it's best to stay out of it.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ROCK_4">[ Empty beacon (Rock) ]

There's not much at this beacon. Just a few abandoned depots, stripped clean.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ROCK_5">[ Empty beacon (Rock) ]

A few freighters pass by but they refuse all communications. Must not want to sully their reputation by talking with foreigners.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ROCK_6">[ Empty beacon (Rock) ]

You see a small trading post and ask about refuelling but they respond, "Go away! We don't serve your kind here."</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ROCK_7">[ Empty beacon (Rock) ]

You see a Zoltan merchant and ask about his wares. He responds, "Sorry, but it took years to gain their trust. I can't be seen communicating with you. I hope you understand." He cuts communications.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_SLUG_1">[ Empty beacon (Slug) ]

You arrive at the beacon and are relieved at the sight of open space. Nebulas are terribly claustrophobic.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_SLUG_2">[ Empty beacon (Slug) ]

This beacon marks a 'small' gap in the nebula. No colonies or ships in scanning distance.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_SLUG_3">[ Empty beacon (Slug) ]

You are relieved to see your sensors blink back on after the jump. No ships detected.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_SLUG_4">[ Empty beacon (Slug) ]

The Slugs rely heavily on their telepathic powers and are reluctant to give up that advantage by extending beyond nebulas. It's unlikely you'll encounter any this far from the clouds.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_SLUG_5">[ Empty beacon (Slug) ]

You arrive in an area clear of nebula and quickly check to see if the sensors are working. Everything is fine and no ships are detected in the vicinity.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ZOLTAN_1">[ Empty beacon (Zoltan) ]

There are some mineral-rich asteroids here that the Zoltan have left idle, but you've none of the necessary equipment to mine them.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ZOLTAN_2">[ Empty beacon (Zoltan) ]

You have to admit - Zoltan space is a beautiful and peaceful place indeed. However, re-engaging the FTL and finishing your mission is your priority, not sight-seeing.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ZOLTAN_3">[ Empty beacon (Zoltan) ]

A light asteroid field is entering the atmosphere of a nearby planet - a fireworks show on a galactic scale. There's little for it but to take in the ambience and program the next jump.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ZOLTAN_4">[ Empty beacon (Zoltan) ]

You stumble upon some Zoltan military vessels engaging in combat training. Their Energy Shields are impressive, but you note how quickly beam and ion weaponry take them down.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ZOLTAN_5">[ Empty beacon (Zoltan) ]

You don't have time to hail the Zoltan ship that was waiting at this beacon before it jumps away. They are a careful race.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ZOLTAN_6">[ Empty beacon (Zoltan) ]

A Zoltan shipyard is stationed at this beacon. You admire the display of hundreds of glowing Zoltan performing delicate exterior work on a massive transport ship.</text>

<text name="text_NOTHING_ZOLTAN_7">[ Empty beacon (Zoltan) ]

A message broadcast from a nearby planet announces the presence of an ancient Zoltan monastery available for visiting. Likely just a tourist trap, but still too bad you don't have the time to visit.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_NOTHING_SLUG_1">[ Empty nebula beacon (Slug) ]

When it comes to Slugs, no news is not necessarily good news. However, if they are watching, they don't seem to want to confront you.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_NOTHING_SLUG_2">[ Empty nebula beacon (Slug) ]

It's not unusual to feel paranoia in a Slug controlled nebula, but for once, it is unfounded.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_NOTHING_SLUG_3">[ Empty nebula beacon (Slug) ]

Either this part of Slug space is deserted, or it's too dense for even Slugs to detect your presence. Time to move.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_NOTHING_SLUG_4">[ Empty nebula beacon (Slug) ]

This area of the nebula seems entirely empty until a small Slug transport and its escorts emerges suddenly from through the clouds, only to disappear again in a matter of seconds.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_NOTHING_SLUG_5">[ Empty nebula beacon (Slug) ]

You explore around the beacon and are shocked when a rock the size of a small moon suddenly looms ahead of you. Scans reveal the solid-looking rock is just a husk, almost entirely mined out of useful minerals.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_NOTHING_SLUG_6">[ Empty nebula beacon (Slug) ]

There are a number of small stations for travellers in the area, lit up by guiding lights and advertisements. Only Slug ships are docked so you decide it's better to avoid a confrontation and steer clear.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_EMPTY_LIST_1">[ Empty nebula beacon ]

You can't see anything through the thick gases surrounding your ship. Without knowing what is out there, all you can do is wait for your FTL to charge.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_EMPTY_LIST_2">[ Empty nebula beacon ]

Without active sensors you have no other option but to look out of the view-ports in apprehension. It's eerily quiet.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_EMPTY_LIST_3">[ Empty nebula beacon ]

As you wait for the FTL drive to charge, you half expect to be ambushed at any moment. However, no attack comes...</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_EMPTY_LIST_4">[ Empty nebula beacon ]

You feel naked without functioning sensors. You half expect a Rebel ship to appear from behind a cloud at any moment, but none come.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_EMPTY_LIST_5">[ Empty nebula beacon ]

Your crew are constantly looking out of the windows, checking for hostiles. They jump at every creak and moan of the ship. The tension is almost palpable...</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_EMPTY_LIST_6">[ Empty nebula beacon ]

You nervously glance out the windows but the only thing to greet you is more clouds and silence.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_EMPTY_LIST_7">[ Empty nebula beacon ]

You cycle through wide-band comm channels as soon as you arrive. Nothing but static.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_EMPTY_LIST_8">[ Empty nebula beacon ]

With the sensors down, you spend a good deal of time staring out the window. It is, you must admit, rather beautiful here.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_EMPTY_LIST_9">[ Empty nebula beacon ]

There's nothing here, save for vast swirls of gas reflecting rays from a distant sun.</text>

<text name="event_FEDERATION_PLANET_SIGNAL_text">[ Encrypted federation signal ]

A Federation encrypted signal is being broadcast from a nearby planet.</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_FLEET_DELAY_text">[ Engi cache ]

You notice an Engi colony hiding on the other side of a nearby moon. It turns out they're excavating an equipment cache from the Federation-Mantis War, and they suggest it might be used to lure the pursuing rebel fleet.</text>

<text name="event_DISTRESS_ENGI_REBEL_text">[ Engi distress Rebel fight ]

The distress signal originates from a small Engi ship under attack by a rebel fighter - but when the Rebels see Federation markings they turn to attack!</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_ENGI_text">[ Engi fight ]

You jump into a debris field that used to be a Zoltan cruiser. Unfortunately, its Engi escort takes you for the attacker and retaliates! They refuse all hails.</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_UNLOCK_1_text">[ Engi fleet discussion ]

You arrive near a small fleet of civilian Engi ships. A simple decryption and translation of their comm frequency tells you that they are having a frantic discussion about something obviously troubling them.</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_MONSTER_text">[ Engi monster ]

As you jump in you're hailed urgently by an Engi science vessel in the distance. "We propose that you do not see the creature." There's nothing on the scanner, which is when you realize you can't see the creature because you're inside it!</text>

<text name="event_DISTRESS_ENGI_REACTOR_text">[ Engi research station ]

You arrive at a smoldering Engi research station, its distress call unanswered - attacked by pirates or Mantis most likely. There may be someone left alive, or else something of value left on board.</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_STATION_DISTRESS_text">[ Engi ship attacked by Mantis ship ]

You receive a distress call from a nearby Engi ship. "Assistance requested. Danger present. Imminent destruction."</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_SEX_text">[ Engi smashed ships ]

What appeared to be a single damaged ship is in fact two ships that have smashed into each other... there is a flurry of comm signals and damage, and it's hard to determine what occurred. The vessels appear to be... Engi? They look locked together by the impact and can't free themselves.</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_SURRENDER_text">[ Engi surrender ]

An Engi ship in the vicinity, seeing you jump in armed to the teeth, immediately broadcasts its surrender: "Subject goal: wealth. Engi motivation: survival. Transfer of goods acceptable?"</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_UNLOCK_2FAKE_SURRENDER_text">[ Engi unlock - decoy base surrender ]

"Stop! I don't want to die here."</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_UNLOCK_2FAKE_text">[ Engi unlock - decoy Rebel base ]

You arrive at one of the Rebel bases that the Engi told you about. It appears abandoned except for one scout ship. Perhaps you could extract information from them.</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_UNLOCK_2REAL_SURRENDER_text">[ Engi unlock - real base surrender ]

"Stop! This isn't worth dying for..."</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_UNLOCK_2REAL_text">[ Engi unlock - real Rebel base ]

You arrive at one of the Rebel bases that the Engi told you about. It appears abandoned except for one scout ship. Perhaps you could extract information from them.</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_UNLOCK_3_text">[ Engi unlock - the cargo escort ]

You have finally caught up with the ships you've been hunting. A hangar-sized cargo ship is being escorted by a number of Mantis ships. As you reconsider the assault, a squadron of Engi ships with pirate emblems jump in and assist you. You prepare to fight the Mantis but scans indicate they are manned by Rebels!</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_UNLOCK_4_text">[ Engi unlock - Project X-ME56 ]

The Engi emerge victorious from their battles with only minor losses. They message you, "Project X-ME56 commissioned by Federation military research division. Advanced stealth cruiser. Project finished during rebellion. Unable to reconnect with Federation military command."</text>

<text name="event_MANTIS_CREW_text">[ Escape pod ]

You detect and retrieve an escape pod floating nearby. You consider returning it to space when you learn it's Mantis.</text>

<text name="event_ESCORT_BEACON_text">[ Escort civilians FTL haywire ]

Once you arrive at the location of the distress call a civilian ship hails you, "Thanks for responding to our beacon. Our FTL navigation has gone haywire and we can't plot a course to the nearest depot to get it fixed. Could you lead us there?"</text>

<text name="text_QUEST_ESCORT_TEXT_1">[ Escort civilians ]

After a short time you receive a message, "Hello. I hope it's not a bother, but I'm looking for an escort to a nearby system. This region is quite dangerous and our ship is not well-armed."</text>

<text name="text_QUEST_ESCORT_TEXT_2">[ Escort civilians ]

There is a single ship at this beacon. They hail you, "We could really use some help. Our FTL navigation system is shot. Can you help us get to a nearby station where they can patch us up?"</text>

<text name="text_QUEST_ESCORT_TEXT_3">[ Escort civilians ]

"Hello," your communicator opens a hail from a nearby ship. "Our weapon systems are malfunctioning and we're too afraid of pirates to travel home unassisted. Can you escort us?"</text>

<text name="event_FEDERATION_BASE_text">[ Federation Base ]

You arrive near the Federation Base to find the bulk of their fleet skirmishing with Rebel forces. You hang back near the far side of the moon to avoid the conflict. There's not much you can do to help in that battle, and your mission holds the key to turn the tide of the war. You prepare to face the Flagship.</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_FED_DESERTER_text">[ Federation deserters ]

For a moment you assume it's a glitch, but no... you've found a Federation military ship! They hail you and, after some probing, reveal that they deserted the Federation fleet before stumbling into this sector while seeking refuge.</text>

<text name="text_BOSS_SCOUT_1">[ Fight in Last Stand ]

Although this sector is still under Federation control, a small scout has slipped by the fleet. You move in to engage.</text>

<text name="text_BOSS_SCOUT_2">[ Fight in Last Stand ]

Long range scanners show this system is empty of any capital ships. Clearly it is not of strategic value. Wait... FTL signatures show a Rebel scout just jumped nearby!</text>

<text name="text_BOSS_SCOUT_3">[ Fight in Last Stand ]

Sensors indicate that the Rebels are setting up a forward Jump Beacon behind the nearby planet's moon. More importantly, a number of ships are passing by; prepare for a fight!</text>

<text name="text_BOSS_SCOUT_4">[ Fight in Last Stand ]

Federation ships are scarce in this region of space despite a number of civilian space stations. You see a small bomber squadron engaged with some Federation scouts and quickly move in to assist.</text>

<text name="text_BOSS_SCOUT_5">[ Fight in Last Stand ]

As soon as you arrive at the beacon, a Rebel scout turns to engage. Power up the weapons!</text>

<text name="text_BOSS_SCOUT_6">[ Fight in Last Stand ]

You scan the area, finding signatures for only a small trade vessel. However, as it approaches you see the silhouette of a Rebel scout! You run the scanners again and discover their registration is fake. You move in to attack.</text>

<text name="event_FINISH_BEACON_NEBULA_text">[ Long-Range Beacon in a nebula (sector exit) ]

This Long-Range Beacon is almost hidden within a nebula. When the FTL Drive is charged you can jump to the next Sector.</text>

<text name="event_FINISH_BEACON_text">[ Long-Range Beacon (sector exit) ]

You've arrived at the Long-Range Beacon. When the FTL Drive is charged you can jump to the next Sector.</text>

<text name="event_DISTRESS_STATION_FIRE_text">[ Fire on research station ]

You find the source of the distress call, a small research station. It appears a small laboratory fire got out of control and is threatening to destroy the station. Their fire suppression system is not responding.</text>

<text name="text_FIND_DRONE_1">[ Free drone schematic ]

When you ask a nearby station for aid, a friendly programmer gives you the schematics for a drone!</text>

<text name="text_FIND_DRONE_2">[ Free drone schematic ]

An abandoned space station circles a lonely planet. A quick check yields schematics for a drone. You bring it aboard the ship.</text>

<text name="text_FIND_DRONE_3">[ Free drone schematic ]

Federation sympathizers contact you as you arrive. "We know your mission should be secret, so don't ask how we know about it. Take this schematic, it's all we can do to help."</text>

<text name="text_FIND_DRONE_4">[ Free drone schematic ]

A small Engi research vessel is trying to fend off a Mantis ship. You move in to engage, but after a quick scan of your ship the Mantis ship retreats. The Engi offer you a drone schematic as thanks for your timely arrival.</text>

<text name="text_FIND_DRONE_5">[ Free drone schematic ]

You find an abandoned mining station on a nearby moon. A quick scan shows no life forms; however, you discover a usable drone schematic!</text>

<text name="text_FIND_DRONE_6">[ Free drone schematic ]

You receive a wide-band message, "Free schematic samples! Be sure to visit our new military-grade drone store opening in sector XR1-45!"</text>

<text name="text_ENGI_GIFT_1">[ Free scrap with resources (Engi) ]

An Engi vessel hails you. "Identity: Federation? Outlier probability. Implies... revival. Implies... hope. Assistance suggested." They offer some supplies.</text>

<text name="text_ENGI_GIFT_2">[ Free scrap with resources (Engi) ]

You cross paths with an Engi cargo vessel hurrying home before the Mantis fleets attempt to take over this sector. They're happy to offload some of their cargo to get home faster.</text>

<text name="text_ENGI_GIFT_3">[ Free scrap with resources (Engi) ]

You make contact with an isolated Engi science station who are staying put despite the likelihood of Mantis invasion. They suggest you trial some experimental technology.</text>

<text name="text_ENGI_GIFT_4">[ Free scrap with resources (Engi) ]

This was the site of a recent battle. Either a show of Mantis force, or the Engi here weren't disposed to go peacefully. You pick through the pieces.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_FREE_STUFF_text">[ Free scrap with resources (Lanius) ]

You stumble across a badly damaged Lanius craft. It jumps away as soon as it sees you. Looking around the area, you discover a number of destroyed Rebel automated ships. It must have been quite the fight. You scrap what remains.</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_DISTRESS_SHELL_text">[ Free scrap with resources (Zoltan) ]

You arrive to find a lumbering Zoltan freighter with no one at the helm. It's a mystery what happened to the crew, but it'd be a shame to let the opportunity go to waste.</text>

<text name="text_FREE_ITEMS_1">[ Free scrap with resources ]

You arrive in a system and immediately discover a pirate ship nearby. Strangely, scans indicate there are no lifeforms aboard. You salvage anything useful, but find no clue as to the whereabouts of the former crew.</text>

<text name="text_FREE_ITEMS_2">[ Free scrap with resources ]

Not much remains in this abandoned system; however, scans reveal a nearby mining platform with some salvageable materials.</text>

<text name="text_FREE_ITEMS_3">[ Free scrap with resources ]

As you arrive in the system you are hailed by a loyalist settlement. Upon learning of your quest, they offer you supplies.</text>

<text name="text_FREE_ITEMS_4">[ Free scrap with resources ]

Debris from a forgotten battle still orbits the gas giant in this system. Some of it still might be usable.</text>

<text name="text_FREE_ITEMS_5">[ Free scrap with resources ]

You receive a message from a nearby station, "A Federation cruiser jumping into Rebel territory? Quite the bold move." You quickly move to arm the weapons but he continues, "Lucky for you we're not all in support of the Rebellion. Perhaps these supplies will help you get to friendlier space alive."</text>

<text name="text_FREE_ITEMS_6">[ Free scrap with resources ]

You happen upon the remains of a space station. It has been mostly picked clean but there appears to be a few materials that will aid you in your mission.</text>

<text name="text_FIND_WEAPON_1">[ Free weapon ]

Holy crap! A weapon is just floating in space!</text>

<text name="text_FIND_WEAPON_2">[ Free weapon ]

You inform a nearby station of your flight from the Rebels. They offer to outfit your ship with a weapon and wish you well.</text>

<text name="text_FIND_WEAPON_3">[ Free weapon ]

A settlement still loyal to the Federation hails your ship. They have prepared a weapon to aid your escape from the Rebels.</text>

<text name="text_FIND_WEAPON_4">[ Free weapon ]

As soon as you arrive a small Mantis ship detaches from a wreck and jumps away. You must have interrupted their salvage operation because you find a weapon ready to be installed!</text>

<text name="text_FIND_WEAPON_5">[ Free weapon ]

A small merchant ship messages you, "Underground Federation comm channels are all talking about your 'secret' mission. Let us install a weapon to help. Good luck!"</text>

<text name="text_FIND_WEAPON_6">[ Free weapon ]

Debris from a battle is scattered around this system. A few pieces bounce against your ship. You passively scan them and discover there is a functioning weapon among them!</text>

<text name="text_FRIENDLY_BEACON_1">[ Friendly ship out of fuel ]

"Greetings! It is so good to see you! We've been out of fuel and floating out here for weeks. We were terrified a pirate or those damn Rebels would find us first. Could you spare some fuel?"</text>

<text name="text_FRIENDLY_BEACON_2">[ Friendly ship out of fuel ]

You arrive to find a ship floating among some debris. "Hello. Our impulse drives are shot and we can't jump. Could you give us some fuel?"</text>

<text name="text_FRIENDLY_BEACON_3">[ Friendly ship out of fuel ]

A small civilian ship flies over as soon as you arrive. You're prepared to fight but they just inform you that they're out of FTL fuel and can't jump.</text>

<text name="text_FRIENDLY_BEACON_4">[ Friendly ship out of fuel ]

"Hello. We used our last FTL fuel to jump to this station." They indicate a burnt out husk of debris and warped metal. "As you can see the war must have spread to this sector. We've been stranded ever since."</text>

<text name="text_FRIENDLY_BEACON_5">[ Friendly ship out of fuel ]

The ship emitting the distress beacon messages you, "Sorry to bother you, but we're out of fuel and can't get out of this barren sector. Could you help us out?</text>

<text name="event_FUEL_ESCAPE_ASTEROIDS_text">[ Fuel escape (asteroid field) ]

While waiting, you managed to navigate out of the asteroid field using only your impulse engines.</text>

<text name="event_FUEL_ESCAPE_STORM_text">[ Fuel escape (ion storm) ]

The ion storm died down, leaving your ship in peace as you wait for help.</text>

<text name="event_FUEL_ESCAPE_SUN_text">[ Fuel escape (sun) ]

While waiting for help, you drained what little power you had left to pull away to a safe distance from the sun.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DISTRESS_LIST_1">[ Fuel fleet distress ]

As you are keeping a low profile, you're certain that the Rebel fleet is having a hard time tracking your ship.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DISTRESS_LIST_2">[ Fuel fleet distress ]

Since your distress beacon has not been activated, you feel confident that the Rebel fleet is having difficulty tracking you. It should buy you a little time.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DISTRESS_LIST_3">[ Fuel fleet distress ]

Long range scanners indicate the Rebel fleet has temporarily paused its advance on your position. Your decision to leave the distress beacon deactivated was farsighted.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DISTRESS_LIST_4">[ Fuel fleet distress ]

Scanners show that the Rebel fleet has ceased its pursuit for a short time.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DISTRESS_LIST_5">[ Fuel fleet distress ]

Your intuition as captain is telling you that the Rebels are having a hard time trying to find your ship.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DISTRESS_LIST_6">[ Fuel fleet distress ]

Without a distress beacon or any FTL signatures to trace, you're sure that the Rebels are struggling to find you. You can only hope their confusion lasts until more fuel can be found.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DISTRESS_LIST_7">[ Fuel fleet distress ]

The Rebel fleet seems to be unable to locate your ship's signature. If only you could get some fuel, you might still have a chance to place some distance between you and the Rebels...</text>

<text name="event_FUEL_OFF_ROCK_CURIOUS_text">[ No fuel: curious Rock ship ]

A curious Rock ship comes in for a closer look at you. They refuse all hails.</text>

<text name="text_GHOST_SHIP_TEXT_1">[ Ghost ship ]

This beacon lies in an empty section of space. You almost move on before spotting a heavily damaged ship drifting nearby. The ship's markings are unfamiliar.</text>

<text name="text_GHOST_SHIP_TEXT_2">[ Ghost ship ]

You share this beacon with just one other ship, but it appears ancient and long since abandoned.</text>

<text name="text_GHOST_SHIP_TEXT_3">[ Ghost ship ]

Another ship is jumping away just as you arrive. They send out a quick communication before their jump completes: "That ruined bulk is more trouble than it's worth." You see a drifting, abandoned vessel nearby.</text>

<text name="text_GHOST_SHIP_TEXT_4">[ Ghost ship ]

There's a heavily damaged ship at this beacon. You briefly pick up a very distorted communication from the ship but are unable to understand it. Your sensors detect no life-signs.</text>

<text name="event_DISTRESS_INFESTATION_text">[ Giant alien spiders ]

You find a number of ships fleeing from a small space station. You hail them, asking what's wrong: "Help! We're being overrun by some sort of giant alien spiders!"</text>

<text name="text_TRADER_UPGRADES_EXCHANGE_TEXT_1">[ Improve reactor for supplies ]

"You look like a military vessel. We're trying to get back to our homes alive. I'm an engineer by trade and could try to improve your reactor if you have any extra supplies."</text>

<text name="text_TRADER_UPGRADES_EXCHANGE_TEXT_2">[ Improve reactor for supplies ]

You receive a message from a small convoy. They're looking for some military supplies and are offering to try to improve your reactor in exchange.</text>

<text name="event_DONOR_PONY_text">[ Intelligent ponies ]

Scanners are showing intelligent life forms on a nearby planet. No match for them can be found in the database.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_RESEARCHER_CRAFT_text">[ Lanius craftsmen ]

A merchant ship is docked with a Lanius transport. You message them to see if they need any help. It turns out they have been studying the Lanius's ability to reshape metal.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_DISTRESS_EMPTY_text">[ Lanius empty distress beacon 1 ]

You arrive at the location of the distress signal prepared for a fight, but on first glance it's entirely empty. The signal is coming from a small plastic satellite orbiting a moon. A looping message describes how settlers have recently abandoned the area due to the Lanius threat. You fail to find any other signs of a settlement nearby.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_DISTRESS_TOOLATE_text">[ Lanius empty distress beacon 2 ]

When you get to the beacon you quickly try to locate the source of the distress call. As you are looking, the signal blinks out. It is then that you notice the small fleet of scavenger ships absorbing debris from a large battle nearby. You can't help but wonder where the distress signal came from, but you decide not to risk pressuring the fleet.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_DISTRESS_TRAP_text">[ Lanius fight distress ]

You are too late - whatever once was emitting the distress signal from this system drew a Lanius ship as well as your own. Having consumed the original target, the Lanius turn their attention to your vessel.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_FIGHT_ASTEROID_text">[ Lanius fight in asteroid field ]

This beacon appears to have been set up within an asteroid field to access a mining settlement. However, half of the settlement has been disassembled by a number of Lanius scavengers. Their military escort moves in to scare you off.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_FIGHT_PULSAR_text">[ Lanius fight near pulsar ]

There appears to be some sort of research station near a pulsar, although it's hard to tell since a portion of it has been melted. The Lanius ship that has been working at it moves in to intercept you, totally oblivious to the threat of EM pulses.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_NOBOARDERS_PDS_text">[ Lanius fight with friendly ASB support ]

Upon arrival you are immediately surrounded by chaos: a planet's Anti-Ship Battery is firing on a number of Lanius ships; one of the combat ships mistakenly believes your ship has arrived to assist the planetary defenses. Combat positions!</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_SCARED_CIVILIAN_text">[ Lanius lone ship ]

You arrive at the beacon to discover a civilian ship fleeing from a lone Lanius craft. The civilian messages you, "Help! The metal monsters are coming to melt down our ship!" Strangely, no active weapon signatures are detected.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_DORMANT_EVENT_text">[ Lanius powered-down ship ]

You have picked up a Lanius vessel drifting in this sector. There is no damage to the hull, and it appears to be powered down.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_AUTO_REBEL_text">[ Lanius ship absorbing automated scout ]

You come across a Lanius ship in the process of absorbing a Rebel automated scout. If you scare off the Lanius you could probably make use of it.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_BEACON_EATER_text">[ Lanius ship absorbing jump beacon ]

You detect a damaged vessel docked with the jump beacon. It appears the Lanius are absorbing metal from the beacon, risking destroying it and becoming stranded.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_GROUP_AUTO_text">[ Lanius ship absorbing rebel base ]

You notice a number of Lanius ships absorbing a forward Rebel base and its automated scouts. They don't seem to be aggressive. Perhaps their desire for metal could prove to be useful?</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_DISTRESS_FIGHT_text">[ Lanius ship attacking civilian distress ]

You immediately do a short-range scan after arriving at the beacon. It appears to be coming from a small civilian vessel under fire from a Lanius ship. Not all Lanius are content with simply scavenging the wrecks of previous battles.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_CIVILIAN_TEXT_1">[ Lanius ship attacking civilian ]

You immediately receive a message upon arrival, "Help! These metal bastards have gone crazy!" The communication originates from the hull of a partially dismantled ship which lies among a number of other destroyed ships. The violent Lanius ship responsible for this carnage is advancing on the survivors.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_CIVILIAN_TEXT_2">[ Lanius ship attacking civilian ]

You scan the area after arriving at this system. A Lanius ship is in fast pursuit of an unarmed civilian ship. It's hard to say if it's truly a threat since its weapons are not charging.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_CIVILIAN_TEXT_3">[ Lanius ship attacking civilian ]

You arrive at the location of a recent battle. Judging from the debris, some settlers attempted to fight off a number of small Lanius ships, although it's impossible to say who instigated the aggression. A few skirmishes can be seen in the distance, but more notably a lone Lanius ship is firing on a heavily damaged civilian vessel.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_MANTIS_DISTRESS_text">[ Lanius ship attacking Mantis ]

The Mantis ship in this system looks like its distress beacon is malfunctioning... likely due to the Lanius ship mining their hull and sub-systems! It doesn't look like the Mantis ship will last much longer.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_ROCK_DISTRESS_text">[ Lanius ship attacking Rock ]

A distress beacon pulses weakly from a Rockman ship in this system... their hull (and their crew) are being mined by the Lanius, lasers and weapons tearing through the ship!</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_SLUG_DISTRESS_text">[ Lanius ship attacking Slug ]

The distress signal from this system is coming from a Slug vessel under attack by the Lanius! The Slugs beg for assistance as the Lanius tear into their hull plating.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_HARVESTER_text">[ Lanius ship in rich debris field ]

Your scans have picked up a Lanius vessel in this system: it appears to be navigating a rich debris field, harvesting the minerals.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_SURRENDER_TEXT_1">[ Lanius surrender ]

An image of a silent Lanius captain appears on your monitor. Images of their well-filled cargo hold follow. You come to the conclusion that they are trying to barter for a cease-fire.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_SURRENDER_TEXT_2">[ Lanius surrender ]

The Lanius ship hails you. Your translator struggles, spurting out "Prevent death... Merciful... Penitent...". You believe they are surrendering.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_SURRENDER_TEXT_3">[ Lanius surrender ]

You receive a hail from the ship followed by a crude translation device spurting, "Stop. Stop. Stop."</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_SURRENDER_TEXT_4">[ Lanius surrender ]

You receive an image of their captain, silhouetted by the destruction aboard their ship. It bows forward with the metallic appendages about its body doing the same. It appears to be requesting mercy.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_SURRENDER_TEXT_5">[ Lanius surrender ]

Your comms system receives a video feed of the enemy ship's crew waving small makeshift white flags. It appears they have taken research about your culture's customs quite literally.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_SURRENDER_TEXT_6">[ Lanius surrender ]

You receive a message from the enemy ship that your translator struggles to interpret, "Penitence for metal. Offering intention."</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_SURRENDER_TEXT_7">[ Lanius surrender ]

You receive a one word message from the enemy ship, "Surrender." You assume they are asking to surrender rather than demanding your surrender.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_TRADER_TRANSLATOR_text">[ Lanius trader with translator ]

A Lanius merchant appears to have a significantly improved translator as you clearly understand their message. "Metal content more than sufficient. Does your ship care to exchange resources for our excess metal?"</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_TRADER_TEXT_1">[ Lanius trader ]

Aided by a modified translator, a nearby Lanius scavenger ship messages you, saying, "Metal sufficient. Request exchange." It appears there are some Lanius who wish sociable interaction with other races.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_TRADER_TEXT_2">[ Lanius trader ]

A small Lanius craft approaches. You prepare for a fight but they do not seem to be carrying any weapons. After a brief moment they message you, although your translator struggles with the unfamiliar dialect. It appears they wish to trade.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_TRADER_TEXT_3">[ Lanius trader ]

You arrive to find a large Lanius vessel laden with recently collected metal. They are apparently offering to trade for supplies they are lacking.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_RESEARCHER_CONTACT_text">[ Lanius with Federation science craft ]

A Federation science craft is docked with a few Lanius ships. You hail them and ask what is going on. "Greetings! We have been attempting to understand our region's newest visitors, the Lanius, although we have been making little headway in deciphering their language."</text>

<text name="event_ASTEROID_EXPLORE_text">[ Large asteroid field ]

Scans reveal a large asteroid field nearby. Short-range scanners may discover useful materials while we wait for the FTL to recharge.</text>

<text name="event_STORE_REBELSIDE_text">[ Large trade station ]

You come across a large trade station. However, as soon as you approach a warning goes out to all ships in the region: "Do not associate with the Federation sympathizer. All who oppose the Rebels will be punished."</text>

<text name="event_LAST_STAND_START_text">[ Last Stand start ]

You arrive at an outpost close to the Federation Base. Your access codes get you past initial security and an officer sets up a direct feed to the Federation Base's war room. Admiral Tully speaks first saying, "What is the meaning of this?! Who are you?"</text>

<text name="event_MANTIS_NAMED_THIEF_text">[ Legendary thief KazaaakplethKilik ]

You cross paths with a Mantis ship that looks to have had dozens of layers of armor-plating added over what must have been a hundred year career. Its captain is legendary thief KazaaakplethKilik. Your crew look frightened.</text>

<text name="event_DISTRESS_SATELLITE_DEFENSE_text">[ Malfunctioning defense system ]

The distress signal is coming from a small space station orbiting an uninhabited planet. Their satellite defense system has gone haywire and their repair crew can't approach without being fired on. They're looking for help to fix or disable it.</text>

<text name="event_MANTIS_CAPTURE_COMMANDO_text">[ Mantis capture commando ]

You come across an Engi wreck with one life-sign aboard; it turns out to be the sole survivor of the Mantis boarding party that wiped out the ship's crew. He's in no state to fight and he's brought aboard.</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_MANTIS_CHOICE_text">[ Mantis fight choice in nebula ]

Navigating the fog blind, you practically bump hulls with a Mantis ship. They hail you: "Pah! This transgression will be overlooked. Nebula, very dangerous. Next time, humans all die."</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_CHOICE_1">[ Mantis fight choice ]

You're greeted by a rare sight: a Mantis ship that appears not to have noticed you.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_CHOICE_2">[ Mantis fight choice ]

For once, you see the Mantis before they see you.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_CHOICE_3">[ Mantis fight choice ]

When they see the Mantis warship waiting in ambush at your intended coordinates, your crew is relieved to note you've jumped someway off the mark.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_CHOICE_4">[ Mantis fight choice ]

You overhear Mantis comm chatter: "Negative, I have killed more humans!" You gulp noticeably, but luckily they don't see you yet.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_CHOICE_5">[ Mantis fight choice ]

You overhear Mantis comm chatter: "The one on the right is starting to rot. Take him down. Take off his fingers. Put him out of the airlock." They certainly don't seem to be friendly...</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_CHOICE_6">[ Mantis fight choice ]

You overhear Mantis comm chatter: "Agreed. Next ship is your turn. Good hunting." They don't see you yet.</text>

<text name="text_ENGI_MANTIS_FIGHT_1">[ Mantis fight (Engi) ]

A mixed radar signal turns out to be a Mantis attack ship scavenging the remains of an Engi carrier. They turn and fight.</text>

<text name="text_ENGI_MANTIS_FIGHT_2">[ Mantis fight (Engi) ]

You come across a Mantis raider taking pot shots at a defenceless Engi supply station. Discovering its weapons aren't much of a match for the station's armour, it turns on your ship. Battle stations!</text>

<text name="text_ENGI_MANTIS_FIGHT_3">[ Mantis fight (Engi) ]

The area looks clear, and you prepare to jump off, but a Mantis scout jumps in behind you! They're as surprised as you are, but their weapons are already online.</text>

<text name="text_ENGI_MANTIS_FIGHT_4">[ Mantis fight (Engi) ]

You find a Mantis ship harrying a small squad of Engi. They make it to the node and jump off, leaving you toe to toe with their pursuer!</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_SLUG_MANTIS_text">[ Mantis fight in nebula (Slug) ]

The Mantis attack ship here looks to have been hunting Slugs on their home turf - a rare test of honor for the mightiest Mantis crews. Weapons up!</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_MANTIS_FIGHT_1">[ Mantis fight in nebula ]

Nebulas are known to be popular Mantis hunting grounds. Information you would have done well to heed here.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_MANTIS_FIGHT_2">[ Mantis fight in nebula ]

You detect a Mantis expedition vessel returning home with its haul. So determined are they, in fact, that they don't wait to see if you're hostile before firing.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_MANTIS_FIGHT_3">[ Mantis fight in nebula ]

A Mantis ship, lost in the storm, hails you. "Sensors are out. We have no local telemetry. We will take yours." You detect a power increase in their weapons systems.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_MANTIS_FIGHT_4">[ Mantis fight in nebula ]

A Mantis ship hails you through the storm: "These are sacred Urggghtnag clan hunting grounds. You are prey." Shields up!</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_MANTIS_FIGHT_5">[ Mantis fight in nebula ]

You notice a Mantis attack ship ducking between the clouds of swirling space stuff; it's hunting you. You try to get the jump and move in to attack.</text>

<text name="event_MANTIS_SUN_FIGHT_text">[ Mantis fight near sun ]

Who knows why the Mantis would venture so close to a sun. Perhaps it makes for more of a challenge?</text>

<text name="event_SLUG_MANTIS_text">[ Mantis fight (Slug) ]

You intercept comm chatter from an incoming Mantis ship. "Look. This ship appears not to be owned by the squishy ones. Maybe they won't smell so bad when we cut them open." They move in on your position.</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_MANTIS_text">[ Mantis fight (Zoltan) ]

You pick up the last broadcast from a rupturing Zoltan freighter: "The Mantis, they're here, please-" You're interrupted by fire off the port bow!</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_1">[ Mantis fight ]

A Mantis military ship appears on local radar alongside the remains of a human freighter. Prepare for a hostile encounter!</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_2">[ Mantis fight ]

A Mantis military scout hails your ship. "Foolish alien! Your kind has stifled our greatness for too long! You will rue the day you backed the Federation!"</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_3">[ Mantis fight ]

A small Mantis cruiser is broadcasting a repeating message on a wide-band frequency, "All non-Mantis ships that enter our territory are forfeit. Lower your shields and surrender if you value your lives."</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_4">[ Mantis fight ]

You detect a small military outpost and a few freighters nearby. This mineral rich planet in an isolated location would be perfect for an illegal Mantis mining operation. As you consider your options, a ship launches from the outpost. Prepare for a fight.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_5">[ Mantis fight ]

You discover yet another unlicensed and uncharted Mantis colony. They certainly waste no time expanding their claims. A Mantis ship moves to intercept you before you can jump away.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_6">[ Mantis fight ]

A Mantis military scout seems to have just finished a salvage op on a nearby wreck. They have no time to waste with warnings and appear to wish to fight.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_7">[ Mantis fight ]

A small military craft hails you and a Mantis captain appears on your receiver. "All local human colonies have been punished for the Federation's transgressions. Submit to processing."</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_8">[ Mantis fight ]

A nearby Mantis ship begins aggressive maneuvers. You prepare for the worst.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_9">[ Mantis fight ]

A stream of clicks and gurgling comes on the comm from a hostile Mantis scout. The universal translator might be on the blink, but his intent is obvious.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_10">[ Mantis fight ]

The Mantis ship is pleased to see you, and fires up its weapon systems.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_11">[ Mantis fight ]

You recognize the outline of a Mantis ship against the blackness. Engage!</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_12">[ Mantis fight ]

Something red looms. It's the Mantis.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_13">[ Mantis fight ]

A Mantis vessel hails you. "This hail is merely a distraction!" You notice their shields and weapons have come online.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_14">[ Mantis fight ]

You notice a flurry of laser fire glance by the port window. The Mantis are upon you.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_15">[ Mantis fight ]

The Mantis hail you. Their captain says, "I claim this vessel for my clan. Good hunting!"</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_16">[ Mantis fight ]

A Mantis female comes on the vidscreen. The females don't make it to authority unless they're particularly vicious. You power the weapons.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_17">[ Mantis fight ]

A Mantis ship with the markings of a warrior tribe breaks position and attacks!</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_18">[ Mantis fight ]

A Mantis ship hails: "Ah! Fine prey. Fine prey! We honor you with our most eviscerating arsenal!" You sense a cloud to this silver lining and power the weapons.</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_19">[ Mantis fight ]

Children on Earth are told terrible tales of the blood red Mantis invasion ships - much like the one bearing down on you now - which once threatened the planet. You order weapons free!</text>

<text name="text_MANTIS_FIGHT_20">[ Mantis fight ]

A youthful-looking Mantis captain hails. "You, prey, must know. Your death, Kaaazthwak's final kill before maturity. Kaaazthwak pay respects." Seems respects in Mantis culture are paid with lasers.</text>

<text name="event_ALISON_MANTIS_CREW_text">[ Mantis fugitive ]

You arrive just in time to see an unusually well-armed Engi ship destroying a small pirate craft. A teleporter signal is detected...intruder on deck!</text>

<text name="event_MANTIS_GAMBLE_text">[ Mantis gamble ]

This node is currently home to a Mantis leisure ship: a place of brothels and combat arenas for warriors to release steam. When they scan your inventory they indicate that you're eligible to engage in a grand game of chance.</text>

<text name="event_MANTIS_NAMED_THIEF_DEFEAT_text">[ KazaaakplethKilik defeated ]

No more life signs are detected aboard their ship. You appear to have won.</text>

<text name="event_MANTIS_NAMED_THIEF_STASH_text">[ KazaaakplethKilik's stash ]

You arrive at small asteroid field and discover the hidden cache among the debris. You input the codes given to you by KazaaakplethKilik and find a weapon inside.</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_BOARDERS_MANTIS_text">[ Mantis outcasts ]

The Mantis outcasts sometimes make the mistake of taking the Zoltan for easy game. A scout moves in to attack while a boarding party beams aboard from a nearby transport!</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_MANTIS_CRYSTAL_text">[ Mantis ship attacking Crystal ]

You discover a number of civilian ships fleeing the area. Shots are fired and you find the assailant; a Mantis ship is attacking one of the smaller ships!</text>

<text name="event_SLUG_DISTRESS_MANTIS_text">[ Mantis ship attacking Slug ship ]

The distress call appears to be emanating from a Slug ship caught in open space by a Mantis raider. They contact you on emergency frequencies: "Please, we'll give you all we have if you sssave ussss!"</text>

<text name="event_DONOR_MANTIS_CHASE_text">[ Mantis ship-collectors ]

You are immediately hailed by an impressive looking Mantis ship, "Your ship would make a mighty fine prize. Prepare for battle!"</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_MANTIS_HUNTER_text">[ Mantis ship with Rock body parts ]

A Mantis ship here is adorned with Rock body parts! It would be a gorier display if they had internal organs, but the message is clear enough: this is a hunter of a very specialized kind.</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_MANTIS_FREIGHTER_text">[ Mantis ships battle for Rock freighter ]

A curious sight greets you at this beacon: a disabled Rock freighter drifts in space while two Mantis craft battle it out - presumably over who deserves the spoils.</text>

<text name="event_QUEST_MANTIS_INVASION_START_text">[ Mantis war camp ]

You receive a request, "All of our military ships have been destroyed or damaged during the rebellion. However, there have been reports of a Mantis war camp only a few jumps from us. Can you help?"</text>

<text name="event_MERCHANT_DELIVER_text">[ Merchant's delivery ]

You arrive at the location given to you by the merchant. You are supposed to deliver drone parts to a station here.</text>

<text name="event_MERCHANT_INVESTIGATE_DELIVER_text">[ Deliver to the station ]

You find the station that had ordered your cargo. You drop it off and they respond, "Ignoring the fact that this is days late, we really appreciate that you delivered our materials. We realize how dangerous this sector is these days. Take this as payment."</text>

<text name="event_MERCHANT_INVESTIGATE_text">[ Merchant's investigation ]

You arrive at the last known location of the merchant's delivery. You begin to scan for the lost ship.</text>

<text name="event_MERCHANT_REQUEST_text">[ Merchant's request ]

You arrive at a populated sector. One merchant seems to be mass-broadcasting a request for a mercenary ship to aid him. Shall we respond?</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_LOST_SHIP_text">[ Nebula lost ship ]

A heavily damaged Federation ship is hiding in the nebula at this beacon. Before you have time to make contact with them, they fade into the nebula.</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_BATTLEFIELD_text">[ Nebula wreckage ]

This nebula looks like it's recently seen two ships exchange fire... with mutually-assured destructive results. Wreckage drifts by your screens and tumbles into the depths of the nebula to be lost to sight. It's hard to determine who the combatants were without closer investigation.</text>

<text name="event_FUEL_ON_REBEL_WARNING_text">[ No fuel: Auto-ship warning ]

A ship responding to your distress moves in. Unfortunately it turns out to be an automated Rebel scout. It immediately reverses thrust after scanning your ship.</text>

<text name="event_FUEL_SELLER_DISTRESS_text">[ No fuel: automated refueling ship ]

A small ship arrives with a message, "This automated ship will provide refueling services once a monetary exchange is complete. Complimentary amounts of fuel are available in emergencies only."</text>

<text name="event_FUEL_OFF_ROCK_WRECK_text">[ No fuel: drifting debris ]

As you await either salvation or death, your attention is drawn to a sea of debris drifting past the starboard view port. The chunks gliding by grow bigger in size until the stern of a Rock frigate, gutted in some distant war, comes into view.</text>

<text name="event_FUEL_OFF_ENGI_DUBIOUS_text">[ No fuel: Engi ship repair ]

As you drift through space an Engi ship passes through. From listening to their com channel it sounds like they're discussing making repairs on their ship.</text>

<text name="event_FUEL_EXPLORE_text">[ No fuel: explore the system ]

Although your lack of fuel cells prevents your ship from jumping, you can still use your impulse engines. Will you spend some time exploring the nearby system?</text>

<text name="event_NO_FUEL_FLEET_DLC_text">[ No fuel: the fleet arrives (AE) ]

Your pilot deftly avoids incoming artillery fire from the surrounding fleet while you try to sort out exactly what your plan is... One of the many approaching fighters gets into weapon range and your scanners detect it has surplus fuel. Maybe you can still pull this off.</text>

<text name="event_NO_FUEL_FLEET_text">[ No fuel: the fleet arrives ]

The Rebel fleet has caught up to you. You detect significant fuel reserves in one of their closer fighters and move in to attack. Maybe you can still pull this off.</text>

<text name="event_NO_FUEL_REFUGEE_FRIENDLY_text">[ No fuel: friendly refugee ]

A refugee ship fleeing the Rebel advance enters the system. It seems surprised to see you stranded, and admits it was following you from afar in the hopes of you leading it to Federation space. While it doesn't have much fuel to spare, it recognizes you are part of the Federation and offers to split its remaining fuel with you.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_TRADER_TEXT_LIST_1">[ No fuel: fuel trader (distress off) ]

A merchant ship jumps into the sector and you quickly hail them asking for help. They respond, "Perhaps we could work out an exchange..."</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_TRADER_TEXT_LIST_2">[ No fuel: fuel trader (distress off) ]

A number of ships pass through the sector. You relay your message to each, and one finally responds. "I can't help much right now but perhaps we can trade."</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_TRADER_TEXT_LIST_3">[ No fuel: fuel trader (distress off) ]

A nearby settlement sends a small ship in your direction. It keeps its distance and hails you, "We can give you fuel for a price. Just don't even think of doing anything rash. We've got a teleporter at our base and a squad ready to defend us.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_TRADER_TEXT_LIST_4">[ No fuel: fuel trader (distress off) ]

A large caravan of merchant ships jumps to a location near your position. Sensing an opportunity, one ship breaks off from the fleet to offer you an exchange.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_TRADER_TEXT_LIST_5">[ No fuel: fuel trader (distress off) ]

A modified YT-1300 freighter jumps to an area near your sector. Your gut tells you these people are smugglers, but they seem to be feeling altruistic and present an offer of assistance.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_TRADER_DISTRESS_TEXT_LIST_1">[ No fuel: fuel trader (distress on) ]

A merchant ship jumps into the sector, obviously responding to your ship's distress beacon. They hail you offering a trade for fuel.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_TRADER_DISTRESS_TEXT_LIST_2">[ No fuel: fuel trader (distress on) ]

A ship arrives at the beacon. "We noticed your distress signal. I assume you're out of fuel? We're a bit low ourselves but perhaps we can make a trade."</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_TRADER_DISTRESS_TEXT_LIST_3">[ No fuel: fuel trader (distress on) ]

A ship traveling near the beacon approaches your ship and hails you. "Out of fuel? This is a good opportunity for both of us... Care to trade?"</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_TRADER_DISTRESS_TEXT_LIST_4">[ No fuel: fuel trader (distress on) ]

A mercenary ship arrives at the beacon. "We have a bit of extra fuel we can give you... for a price."</text>

<text name="event_FUEL_APPROACH_text">[ No fuel: prepare to dock ]

A ship approaches. They hail you saying, "You need some fuel? We'll prepare to dock to help."</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_ON_REBEL_ATTACK_1">[ No fuel: Rebel fight ]

A Rebel ship hails you, "Hello citizen. We are responding to your distress call and can assist... Wait a second... You're that ship! Prepare to die!"</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_ON_REBEL_ATTACK_2">[ No fuel: Rebel fight ]

A Rebel ship jumps nearby, "I wasn't looking forward to patrolling this boring sector but here you are, the most wanted ship in the area, just asking for me to find you. It looks like it's my lucky day!" They power up their weapons.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_ON_REBEL_ATTACK_3">[ No fuel: Rebel fight ]

Your distress beacon must be working because a ship just jumped nearby. You run a scan on it and activate a red alert. It's a Rebel fighter!</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_ON_REBEL_ATTACK_4">[ No fuel: Rebel fight ]

A Rebel ship jumps in and hails you, "I knew you would slip up some time. Surrender quietly!"</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DELAY_LIST_1">[ No fuel: Rebel fleet delay ]

As you are keeping a low profile, you're certain that the Rebel fleet is having a hard time tracking your ship.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DELAY_LIST_2">[ No fuel: Rebel fleet delay ]

Since your distress beacon has not been activated, you feel confident that the Rebel fleet is having difficulty tracking you. It should buy you a little time.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DELAY_LIST_3">[ No fuel: Rebel fleet delay ]

Long range scanners indicate the Rebel fleet has temporarily paused its advance on your position. Your decision to leave the distress beacon deactivated was farsighted.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DELAY_LIST_4">[ No fuel: Rebel fleet delay ]

Scanners show that the Rebel fleet has ceased its pursuit for a short time.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DELAY_LIST_5">[ No fuel: Rebel fleet delay ]

Your intuition as captain is telling you that the Rebels are having a hard time trying to find your ship.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DELAY_LIST_6">[ No fuel: Rebel fleet delay ]

Without a distress beacon or any FTL signatures to trace, you're sure that the Rebels are struggling to find you. You can only hope their confusion lasts until more fuel can be found.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FLEET_DELAY_LIST_7">[ No fuel: Rebel fleet delay ]

The Rebel fleet seems to be unable to locate your ship's signature. If only you could get some fuel, you might still have a chance to place some distance between you and them...</text>

<text name="event_NO_FUEL_REFUGEE_DAMAGED_text">[ No fuel: damaged refugee ]

A refugee ship fleeing the Rebel advance enters the system, having picked up your distress beacon. While it doesn't have much fuel to spare, its hull looks damaged - it is in bad need of scrap and is willing to trade fuel for it.</text>

<text name="event_NO_FUEL_REFUGEE_PIRATE_text">[ No fuel: refugee wanting armaments ]

A refugee ship fleeing the Rebel advance enters the system, having picked up your distress beacon. While it doesn't have much fuel to spare, it is bad need of armaments and is willing to trade for them.</text>

<text name="event_FUEL_ON_SLUG_OVERPRICED_text">[ No fuel: Slug fuel depot ]

A mobile Slugman fuel depot enters scanning range. "My prices are fair, but I ask one thing - do not insult me with negotiation!" You check out his price list.</text>

<text name="event_FUEL_ON_SLUG_CHUCKLE_text">[ No fuel: Slug fuel trader ]

A poorly armed Slug ship cruises by and offers assistance. Their captain seems to be chuckling to himself, perhaps at the prices he's charging.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_LIST_1">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress off) ]

No ship is in scanning range and no one arrives at the beacon.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_LIST_2">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress off) ]

Your waiting yields nothing while the fleet surely gets closer...</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_LIST_3">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress off) ]

A freighter suddenly arrives nearby. They are so close you can almost wave at them, but your hails are ignored and the ship quickly jumps away.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_LIST_4">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress off) ]

Small traffic passes within a short distance of you, but no one responds to your hails.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_LIST_5">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress off) ]

The only ship within hailing range appears to be a civilian vessel. However, it quickly leaves once it picks up your signal.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_LIST_6">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress off) ]

As you wait, a small asteroid storm pelts softly against your shields and hull.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_LIST_7">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress off) ]

You begin to wonder if turning on the beacon would be worth the risk of detection. The fleet slowly approaches.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_LIST_8">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress off) ]

You contemplate the vastness of space.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_LIST_9">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress off) ]

The prolonged wait in empty space is causing tension among the crew. Still no contact.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_LIST_10">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress off) ]

Cabin fever begins to spread among your crew.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_LIST_11">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress off) ]

Long range scanners detect a small settlement, but they refuse all contact.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_DISTRESS_LIST_1">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress on) ]

You contemplate that it is fortunate the ship's life support system does not rely on FTL fuel cells.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_DISTRESS_LIST_2">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress on) ]

Nothing happens. Your calls go unanswered.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_DISTRESS_LIST_3">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress on) ]

The distress beacon's light is the only movement visible outside the ship.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_DISTRESS_LIST_4">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress on) ]

No ships jump into the sector...</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_DISTRESS_LIST_5">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress on) ]

A few passing ships seem oblivious to your distress call and ignore all hails.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_DISTRESS_LIST_6">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress on) ]

A few civilian ships are within scanning range, yet none respond to your calls.</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_NOTHING_DISTRESS_LIST_7">[ No fuel: wait fail (distress on) ]

No ships pass through the area.</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_BRIBER_1">[ Pirate briber ]

You come across a pirate in hot pursuit of an unidentified ship. You quickly receive a transmission from the pirate: "Stay out of this fight and we'll make it worth your while."</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_BRIBER_2">[ Pirate briber ]

An unidentified ship is badly damaged and still being assaulted by a space pirate. The victim begins a distress message until the pirate cuts in and offers to split the bounty if you sit tight.</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_BRIBER_3">[ Pirate briber ]

A missile shoots across your bow when the jump completes. Your scans quickly reveal a ship with pirate markings pursuing an unknown vessel. The pirate hails you: "Damn it, we weren't expecting company. Stay out of this and you could profit."</text>

<text name="event_PIRATE_NO_ESCAPE_text">[ Pirate engine hacker ]

Once you arrive, your screen lights up with warnings. A nearby pirate seems to have advanced hacking tools and they have tried to shut down your engines. Your crew manages to keep them barely operational and you move into attack.</text>

<text name="event_PIRATE_ESCAPE_text">[ Pirate escape ]

The enemy ship appears to be powering up its FTL. It's trying to escape!</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_SLUG_PIRATE_text">[ Pirate fight choice in nebula ]

You're surprised to find a ship without Slug markings stranded all the way out here, and move in to provide assistance. When you see the pirate insignia on the hull you quickly reconsider.</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_PIRATE_FIGHT_text">[ Pirate fight (Engi) ]

There must have been rich pickings for pirates around here up until war broke out. The pirate you encounter here looks worn down, but hungry. You'll have to fight!</text>

<text name="event_PIRATE_ASTEROID_text">[ Pirate fight in asteroid field ]

A pirate ship was lying in wait inside this asteroid field. It immediately moves in to attack.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_PIRATE_1">[ Pirate fight in nebula ]

As you drift through the nebula an unmarked vessel descends from the clouds and into your wake. Their weapons come online.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_PIRATE_2">[ Pirate fight in nebula ]

A pirate ship pulls out of the ether and hails: "You know what I love about this part of the galaxy? The explorers! You always carry such fine loot." They lock weapons.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_PIRATE_3">[ Pirate fight in nebula ]

As you coast through the nebula a pirate ship matches your course and closes the distance. Better to pick your battleground, but beggars can't be choosers.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_PIRATE_4">[ Pirate fight in nebula ]

A hostile vessel descends from out of the nebula. Combat stations!</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_PIRATE_5">[ Pirate fight in nebula ]

You try to read the ID of a ship ahead in the fog, but it's too thick to penetrate. You have your answer when the ship turns, weapons hot!</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_PIRATE_FIGHT_TEXT_1">[ Pirate fight (Lanius) ]

A pirate ship appears to be threatening a small refugee ship near the beacon. Upon seeing you jump in, it turns to approach. The civilian wastes no time and jumps away, but that appears only to harden the pirate's resolve.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_PIRATE_FIGHT_TEXT_2">[ Pirate fight (Lanius) ]

An upgraded pirate ship sits among the remains of a number of Lanius ships. It hails you, "These punks think they can jus' waltz in here into our sector? Obnoxious, right? Well, I'm sure you know the routine, let's do this."</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_PIRATE_FIGHT_TEXT_3">[ Pirate fight (Lanius) ]

Debris from a number of battleships are scattered around the beacon. As you approach the area a pirate ship thrusts itself through the hulks to attack. It must be using the metal to lure the Lanius into a trap.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_PIRATE_FIGHT_TEXT_4">[ Pirate fight (Lanius) ]

The pirate ship patroling this sector has been busy. The debris of several Rebel scouts and at least one civilian ship litter the area. "Welcome, welcome, there's room for one more!" The over-confident pirate hails you as he charges his weapons and moves in to attack.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_PIRATE_FIGHT_TEXT_5">[ Pirate fight (Lanius) ]

The pirate sees you before you see him... prepare for a fight!</text>

<text name="event_PIRATE_SUN_text">[ Pirate fight near sun ]

This beacon has been placed too close to a super-giant class M star! The ship will gradually overheat until you get out of here... or die. A pirate, apparently oblivious to the danger of the sun, moves in to engage.</text>

<text name="text_SLUG_PIRATE_1">[ Pirate fight (Slug) ]

There appears to be a pirate ship nearby. Be on your guard; anyone trying to hunt in Slug territory is either formidable or deeply stupid, and in space, either can be dangerous.</text>

<text name="text_SLUG_PIRATE_2">[ Pirate fight (Slug) ]

"We knew anyone foolish enough to try and sneak through a Slug nebula would stick to open space. Yield your goods and we may let you live." You cut the transmission in lieu of a response.</text>

<text name="text_SLUG_PIRATE_3">[ Pirate fight (Slug) ]

Before you can take a moment's rest from the ever present nebulas in this sector, a pirate ship appears behind you and opens fire.</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_1">[ Pirate fight ]

As you jump into the system a pirate advances on your position. They are refusing all hails. Prepare for a fight.</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_2">[ Pirate fight ]

Soon after arriving in the system you are hailed by a small cruiser. "What good fortune that we happen to run into each other. Nothing personal, but you have some information we need!"</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_3">[ Pirate fight ]

At first it appears you've arrived in an empty system, but a ship appears from behind a planet and hails you: "Haha! I am the dread pirate Tuco, prepare to die!"</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_4">[ Pirate fight ]

The only other ship at this beacon messages you: "Finally, after months of waiting, someone has fallen into our trap!"</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_5">[ Pirate fight ]

You barely have time to register jump completion before your ship warns you of an incoming ship with weapons hot.</text>

<text name="event_PIRATE_CIVILIAN_BEACON_text">[ Pirate ship attacking civilian distress ]

The distress beacon is coming from a civilian ship. It appears it is being chased by a pirate.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_PIRATE_CIVILIAN_TEXT_1">[ Pirate ship attacking civilian (Lanius) ]

You discover an abandoned mining facility in the process of being 'acquired' by the Lanius. However, you immediately receive a call from a civilian transport vessel, "Help! We were trying to escape before the Lanius came only to be caught by pirates!" You see a lone pirate ship boarding the civilian craft.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_PIRATE_CIVILIAN_TEXT_2">[ Pirate ship attacking civilian (Lanius) ]

A pirate ship emerges from hiding after you and another ship jump into the area. Sensors show the pirates ran a quick scan of your ship's weapon system before flying off to pursue the unarmed civilian ship.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_PIRATE_CIVILIAN_TEXT_3">[ Pirate ship attacking civilian (Lanius) ]

A pirate ship is firing on the small ships docked at a refueling station. They are broadcasting on a wide band channel. You catch the captain's rant mid-speed, "...saw you trading with those damned scavengers. I'll show you what happens when you try and undercut the Red Giant gang!"</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_CIVILIAN_1">[ Pirate ship attacking civilian ]

You arrive in the system to see a pirate ship pursuing a civilian ship. You detect messages from the civilian ship on a distress frequency.</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_CIVILIAN_2">[ Pirate ship attacking civilian ]

Scanners indicate that a battle is taking place nearby. It seems that someone is under attack by space pirates.</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_CIVILIAN_3">[ Pirate ship attacking civilian ]

You detect two ships, one chasing the other... Scanners show the pursuer is a pirate!</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_CIVILIAN_4">[ Pirate ship attacking civilian ]

There are only two ships within range and they seem to be engaged in battle. One of them has the markings of a space pirate.</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_CIVILIAN_5">[ Pirate ship attacking civilian ]

You arrive at the next beacon only to be immediately hailed by a small shuttle. "Help us! We are being attacked by pirates!"</text>

<text name="text_PIRATE_CIVILIAN_6">[ Pirate ship attacking civilian ]

You come out of the jump to see laser blasts coming from the other side of the beacon. It looks like someone is under attack from pirates.</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_PIRATE_CRYSTAL_text">[ Pirate ship attacking Crystal ]

A pirate ship jumps in right after you arrive at the beacon. It must have followed once the Long-Range Beacon was reactivated. It almost charges a small Crystalline transport ship, weapons armed.</text>

<text name="text_TRAP_BEACON_TEXT_1">[ Pirate ship distress trap ]

You arrive at the beacon and immediately detect a pirate ship. It seems this distress beacon was a trap!</text>

<text name="text_TRAP_BEACON_TEXT_2">[ Pirate ship distress trap ]

"Haha! I knew someone would fall into our dastardly trap!" It appears this distress beacon was nothing but a decoy for a pirate ambush.</text>

<text name="text_TRAP_BEACON_TEXT_3">[ Pirate ship distress trap ]

Your cockpit lights up with warning signals. You are being targeted by a nearby ship. The distress call was a lure to attract unwitting ships into weapons range. You prepare for a fight.</text>

<text name="text_TRAP_BEACON_TEXT_4">[ Pirate ship distress trap ]

As soon as you arrive at the distress signal, shots are fired toward your ship. A trap!</text>

<text name="event_PIRATE_SALESMAN_text">[ Pirate ship selling drones ]

A ship with conspicuous pirate markings is orbiting a nearby moon, broadcasting a simple message claiming to have equipment available for sale.</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_WEAPONS_TRADER_text">[ Pirate ship selling weapon ]

A black market weapons trader spins you a tale of the dangers of the nebula before pushing his wares.</text>

<text name="event_STORM_ZOLTAN_SUPPLY_CHOICE_text">[ Pirate ships in plasma storm ]

You spy two pirate ships lurking in the nebula here. They remain unaware of your presence; you're able to get your scanners to at least identify their cargo: One is carrying the fuel supplies, the other the ammunition. They begin to drift away from each other in the storm.</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_PIRATE_SMUGGLE_text">[ Pirate smuggler ]

A pirate ship arrives shortly after you. Judging from the fact that it is attempting to avoid your ship, you assume that it's a smuggler trying to stay away from beacons.</text>

<text name="event_PIRATE_SURRENDER_CIVILAN_text">[ Pirate surrender (civilian rescue) ]

The pirates must not have been fully committed to the assault; they have been charging their FTL. They jump away, presumably to repair their ship.</text>

<text name="event_PIRATE_CHOICE_text">[ Pirate toll ]

Upon completing your jump, you receive a message from a nearby ship. "Greetings and welcome to our beacon! For a small fee, we'll let you continue on your way."</text>

<text name="event_DONOR_PLAGUE_text">[ Plagued station ]

You arrive near a damaged and dilapidated space station. It appears to be abandoned but you detect faint life signatures on board.</text>

<text name="event_STORM_ITEMS_text">[ Plasma storm incapacitated ships ]

You jump into the middle of a plasma storm. Multiple recently incapacitated ships loom in the shadows, briefly illuminated by the lightning.</text>

<text name="event_QUEST_CREWDEAD_text">[ Capture the ship - the target ]

You find the ship that you were asked to capture intact. You're not sure why, but they stressed that it's of great importance that you kill the crew WITHOUT destroying the ship.</text>

<text name="event_QUEST_MANTIS_INVASION_text">[ Mantis war camp - the encampment ]

You find the Mantis encampment but there are far too many of them to count accurately. You send a long range message back to the settlement with your findings but unfortunately there's not much you can do. It would be suicide to attack directly.</text>

<text name="event_QUEST_SLUG_PIRATE_TRAP2_text">[ Slug raid, joined ]

You catch up with the two Slug ships and they're already carrying out their raid! One is in close combat with the pirate, the other seems to be heading for a small space cache the pirate was protecting.</text>

<text name="event_QUEST_STORE_RESCUE_text">[ Rescue the space dock ]

Once you arrive at the beacon you detect a Rebel scout assaulting a compound on a nearby desolate moon.</text>

<text name="event_QUEST_STORE_text">[ Hidden space dock ]

You follow the directions given to you and find the hidden space dock. The owner hails you, "I got a message that you were coming. I don't normally offer goods to strangers, but I'll make an exception. Take a look."</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_CHECKPOINT_TEXT_1">[ Rebel checkpoint ]

It looks like this Beacon is home to a Rebel checkpoint. They're stopping and searching any ship that passes through. Civilians are being harassed, and Federation members are detained. The Rebels haven't noticed you yet.</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_CHECKPOINT_TEXT_2">[ Rebel checkpoint ]

Another Rebel checkpoint is monitoring this location. A number of civilian ships are awaiting inspection, any of them could be Federation loyalists. The Rebels haven't noticed you yet.</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_CHECKPOINT_TEXT_3">[ Rebel checkpoint ]

A Rebel space station and single fighter is monitoring this Beacon for Federation activity. A number of civilian ships are docked, awaiting inspection by the Rebels and possible detainment if they are Federation loyalists. The Rebels haven't noticed you yet.</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_CHECKPOINT_TEXT_4">[ Rebel checkpoint ]

A rather large fleet of civilian ships are held up at this Beacon. It appears to be a Rebel checkpoint; everyone is being inspected for possible ties to the Federation. No one has noticed you yet.</text>

<text name="event_ALISON_DEFECTOR_text">[ Rebel defector ]

A Rebel ship is patrolling this beacon, and immediately turns to engage. As your crew scramble to battle readiness, sensors detect a short-range teleporter signal. An intruder is on board!</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_REBEL_CHASE_text">[ Rebel fight chance in nebula ]

You spot a Rebel ship in the nebula ahead and stay off their radar. Try to engage?</text>

<text name="text_ROGUE_REBEL_TEXT_1">[ Rebel fight chance ]

You arrive at a beacon located in a civilian star system. A nearby colony contacts you: "We've got a rogue Rebel ship harassing this system. Do you have time to find it?"</text>

<text name="text_ROGUE_REBEL_TEXT_2">[ Rebel fight chance ]

As soon as you arrive, you receive a Federation encrypted message: A Rebel ship has been terrorizing the local civilians in this system, please seek and destroy it.</text>

<text name="text_ROGUE_REBEL_TEXT_3">[ Rebel fight chance ]

You begin charging your FTL drive, and do a quick scan of a local planet. You find the ruins of a recently destroyed Federation colony of the surface. There must be a Rebel ship in the vicinity...</text>

<text name="text_ROGUE_REBEL_TEXT_4">[ Rebel fight chance ]

You jump into a field of debris. It appears a battle recently took place here, and the loser seems to have been a civilian ship. A message was left on repeat before it was destroyed: "Rebels attacking, please send aid!" The responsible Rebels are likely still nearby.</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_REBEL_UNDETECTED_text">[ Rebel fight choice in nebula ]

Your ship emerges quite far away from the beacon. You see a Rebel ship waiting nearby, undoubtedly stationed to look for you.</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_REBEL_text">[ Rebel fight (Crystal) ]

As soon as you arrive, a Rebel ship jumps in after you; they must be really hot on your tail.</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_REBEL_FIGHT_text">[ Rebel fight (Engi) ]

The rebel fighter here would seem to suggest elements of the rebel fleet are already making incursions on Engi space. You move to engage.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_REBEL_LIST_1">[ Rebel fight in nebula ]

You cross paths with an advance scout of the Rebel fleet searching this section of the nebula for your ship.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_REBEL_LIST_2">[ Rebel fight in nebula ]

A ship bearing Rebel colors can be seen waiting near the beacon. They must have been waiting for you, since they engage immediately.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_REBEL_LIST_3">[ Rebel fight in nebula ]

The Rebels must have anticipated you would try to lose them within the nebula. A scout is waiting for you at the beacon.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_REBEL_LIST_4">[ Rebel fight in nebula ]

It looks like you will be unable to avoid the Rebels by traveling through the nebula. A Rebel ship is waiting for you near the beacon.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_REBEL_LIST_5">[ Rebel fight in nebula ]

Shortly after you arrive, a Rebel ship jumps nearby. There looks to be no escape. Prepare for a fight!</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_REBEL_LIST_6">[ Rebel fight in nebula ]

Newton-knows what brings this Rebel ship so far out; its captain hails, but does a double take when he identifies your ship. They open fire.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_REBEL_LIST_7">[ Rebel fight in nebula ]

A Rebel ship hails, but you don't take chances in conditions like this. You block the frequency and prepare to engage.</text>

<text name="event_STORM_REBEL_text">[ Rebel fight in plasma storm ]

You arrive in the middle of a plasma storm. Despite the harsh conditions, a Rebel scout seems to be waiting for you.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_REBEL_FIGHT_TEXT_1">[ Rebel fight (Lanius) ]

You arrive to see a number of Rebel ships attempting to dissuade Lanius scavenger ships from "acquiring" their forward station. A passing Rebel patrol ship spots you and moves in to intercept.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_REBEL_FIGHT_TEXT_2">[ Rebel fight (Lanius) ]

A Rebel scout patrols near the beacon. "Hah! I knew you would try to sneak through this sector as soon as I heard it had become treacherous. Surrender!"</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_REBEL_FIGHT_TEXT_3">[ Rebel fight (Lanius) ]

You intercept discussions between a Rebel patrol and a human mining colony, "... we realize you're scared but all reports indicate the metal bastards target abandoned settlements only. If we relocated our fleets based on every request from backwater... wait, what's that..." Before you can react, the channel is cut and the Rebel ship moves in to attack.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_REBEL_FIGHT_TEXT_4">[ Rebel fight (Lanius) ]

You arrive at the beacon and notice a small Rebel ship chasing Lanius scavengers away from a wrecked Rebel battleship. As soon as the Rebel notices you and moves in to attack, the Lanius ships return to their prey like flies on garbage.</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_REBEL_FIGHT_TEXT_5">[ Rebel fight (Lanius) ]

A Rebel messages you. "Who would have thought the most wanted ship in the quadrant would just happen by my station? Prepare to meet your maker."</text>

<text name="text_LANIUS_REBEL_FIGHT_TEXT_6">[ Rebel fight (Lanius) ]

Your arrival coincides almost exactly with that of a Rebel ship. It's hard to know who is more surprised, but there is no option but to fight.</text>

<text name="text_SLUG_REBEL_1">[ Rebel fight (Slug) ]

As you arrive at the beacon, a hostile ship immediately registers on your scanners. You didn't expect to see Rebels extending their reach into Slug territory. Charge the weapons!</text>

<text name="text_SLUG_REBEL_2">[ Rebel fight (Slug) ]

You jump into empty space and are relieved to see your sensors blink back to life. However, you are less pleased to see them immediately register a rebel ship on an approach vector!</text>

<text name="text_SLUG_REBEL_3">[ Rebel fight (Slug) ]

You receive a message from a nearby ship, "Looks like our intelligence was correct! Sneaking through the clouds with the Slugs... No one can hide from the rebellion!"</text>

<text name="text_BOARDERS_REBEL_SHIP_1">[ Rebel fight with boarders ]

You receive a message from a nearby Rebel station, "You have a lot of guts passing through our space, I'll give you that." He turns giving an order, "Kill their crew, I want that ship intact."</text>

<text name="text_BOARDERS_REBEL_SHIP_2">[ Rebel fight with boarders ]

Your sensors warn of an incoming Rebel ship at the same time as you hear the telltale signs of a teleporter. You hear someone taunt from within the ship, "Ready to die? I sure am ready to get a promotion!"</text>

<text name="text_BOARDERS_REBEL_SHIP_3">[ Rebel fight with boarders ]

Incoming message, "Hello Captain," says a Rebel in an officer's garb. "How very generous of you to turn yourself in. Prepare to be boarded. Come quietly and we may be lenient."</text>

<text name="text_BOARDERS_REBEL_SHIP_4">[ Rebel fight with boarders ]

You receive a message on a low-band channel. "You're surrounded, just like the last of your Federation friends. Just die already." The enemy has teleported onto your ship!</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_1">[ Rebel fight ]

Your ship is hailed. "We've found you at last. Prepare to die!"</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_2">[ Rebel fight ]

A small Rebel ship is docked at a small station. You try to lay low but it spots you. Power up the weapons!</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_3">[ Rebel fight ]

A Rebel ship has been patrolling this region. As soon as you arrive it begins its assault.</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_4">[ Rebel fight ]

A Rebel ship hails you: "Federation scum! We've waited a long time for this!"</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_5">[ Rebel fight ]

You receive a transmission: "Sorry sir, this is nothing personal but we're under orders." The Rebel ship's weapons go hot.</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_6">[ Rebel fight ]

By the time you notice the Rebel ship behind the beacon, it's too late to avoid a fight.</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_7">[ Rebel fight ]

A Rebel ship hails. "We did not fight a war to let a single Federation ship shatter our dreams of a better galaxy!" He locks weapons.</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_8">[ Rebel fight ]

A Rebel ship approaches cautiously. "Personally," says the captain, "I'd have stuck with the Federation. But I'm a soldier, sir, and I'm no use without a war to fight. Raise your shields!"</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_9">[ Rebel fight ]

You're hailed by a Rebel ship: "When the rebellion is complete you'll see the safer world we provide. Well, you won't, but you get the point." They arm weapons.</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_10">[ Rebel fight ]

A Rebel ship is guarding this beacon. You order a pursuit course and prepare to scratch up one more.</text>

<text name="event_CRYSTAL_REBEL_CRYSTAL_text">[ Rebel ship attacking Crystal ship ]

Crystal shards fly past the screen as soon as you arrive. Checking the scanners, it looks like a crystalline ship is engaged with a Rebel!</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_VS_FEDERATION_1">[ Rebel ship attacking Federation loyalists ]

Upon arriving at this beacon, you detect a distress call. Local scans reveal that a Federation transport is under attack from a Rebel scout!</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_VS_FEDERATION_2">[ Rebel ship attacking Federation loyalists ]

You immediately notice a Rebel ship chasing what appears to be a civilian transport. However you are detecting chatter on an encrypted Federation channel... That transport is carrying Federation loyalists!</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_VS_FEDERATION_3">[ Rebel ship attacking Federation loyalists ]

Your sensors are picking up a distress call on an encrypted Federation channel. You eventually find a Federation scout being chased by a Rebel fighter!</text>

<text name="event_SQUAT_REFUEL_STATION_text">[ Rebel ship attacking refueling outpost ]

You detect a Rebel scout on an attack approach to a small refueling outpost. Their weapons are charged, but they're not firing yet.</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_HELPERS_TEXT_1">[ Rebel ship supplying civilians ]

You stumble across a Rebel ship distributing supplies to local civilian colonies. It's probably not anything military grade, but every little bit helps...</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_HELPERS_TEXT_2">[ Rebel ship supplying civilians ]

You find a Rebel combat ship that has been reassigned as an emergency supply vessel. The local civilians are apparently in need of help, and the Rebels are rising to the occasion.</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_HELPERS_TEXT_3">[ Rebel ship supplying civilians ]

The Rebels in this system are doing supply runs for the local space stations. These civilians have likely been out of supply for months due to the war and are in desperate need.</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_HELPERS_TEXT_4">[ Rebel ship supplying civilians ]

Civilian colonists loyal to the Rebel cause are present on a nearby planet. It looks like they are currently receiving a supply shipment. Could be useful.</text>

<text name="text_REBEL_HELPERS_TEXT_5">[ Rebel ship supplying civilians ]

Because of the war, thousands of colonists have had their supply lines disrupted and have found themselves in dire straits. It seems in this system, the Rebels are sympathetic and are distributing what little supplies they can spare.</text>

<text name="event_SQUAT_WARNING_text">[ Rebel ship warning ]

You stumble across a forward scout of the Rebel fleet.</text>

<text name="event_FLAGSHIP_CONSTRUCTION_text">[ Rebel shipyard ]

You arrive at the beacon to find yourself in a huge Rebel shipyard, scaffolding and construction drones filling the sector! The entire system looks devoted to ship construction, the nearby planets and moons ruthlessly mined to harvest resources for a ship of immense size...</text>

<text name="event_REBEL_TRANSPORT_text">[ Rebel transport ship ]

You spot a small Rebel ship nearby. It seems to have been re-fitted for transport rather than combat. It does not seem to want to engage you and your ship.</text>

<text name="event_LANIUS_FUELING_STATION_text">[ Refueling platform garbled broadcast ]

You detect a refueling platform near the beacon, although its broadcast signal is garbled, and you can't make out the message.</text>

<text name="event_FUELING_STATION_text">[ Refueling platform ]

A small platform orbits near this beacon - it looks like a fueling station of some sort, and it is cheerily broadcasting reasonable prices in a spectrum of frequencies and languages.</text>

<text name="event_REFUEL_STATION_text">[ Refueling station ]

A ship refueling station is stationed at this beacon. We can purchase fuel here.</text>

<text name="event_REFUGEE_GHOST_text">[ Refugee comms down ]

You have encountered a refugee ship drifting in space. It looks as if it was fleeing the Rebel advance and ran out of fuel. Its distress beacon is active, but you're not sure anyone is on board, and its communications seem to be down.</text>

<text name="event_REFUGEE_DISTRESS_PIRATE_text">[ Refugee distress (Pirate) ]

You have encountered a refugee ship drifting in space. It looks as if it was fleeing the Rebel advance and ran out of fuel. Its distress beacon is active, but you're not sure anyone is on board.</text>

<text name="event_REFUGEE_DISTRESS_SLUG_text">[ Refugee distress (Slug) ]

You have encountered a refugee ship drifting in space. It looks as if it was fleeing the Rebel advance and ran out of fuel. Its distress beacon is active, but you're not sure anyone is on board.</text>

<text name="event_REFUGEE_DISTRESS_ZOLTAN_text">[ Refugee distress (Zoltan) ]

You have encountered a refugee ship drifting in space. It looks as if it was fleeing the Rebel advance and ran out of fuel. Its distress beacon is active, but you're not sure anyone is on board.</text>

<text name="event_REFUGEE_DISTRESS_text">[ Refugee distress ]

You have encountered a refugee ship drifting in space. It looks as if it was fleeing the Rebel advance and ran out of fuel. Its distress beacon is active, but you're not sure anyone is on board.</text>

<text name="event_REFUGEE_NO_DISTRESS_PIRATE_text">[ Refugee (Pirate) ]

Your sensors have picked up a refugee ship drifting through the system, no doubt one of many fleeing the Rebel advance. It doesn't appear to have detected you... or else it is trying to avoid notice.</text>

<text name="event_REFUGEE_NO_DISTRESS_SLUG_text">[ Refugee (Slug) ]

Your sensors have picked up a refugee ship drifting through the system, no doubt one of many fleeing the Rebel advance. It doesn't appear to have detected you... or else it is trying to avoid notice.</text>

<text name="event_REFUGEE_TRADER_text">[ Refugee trader ]

The vessel is relieved to hear from you! They are running low on supplies. They suggest a trade.</text>

<text name="event_REFUGEE_NO_DISTRESS_ZOLTAN_text">[ Refugee (Zoltan) ]

Your sensors have picked up a refugee ship drifting through the system, no doubt one of many fleeing the Rebel advance. It doesn't appear to have detected you... or else it is trying to avoid notice.</text>

<text name="event_REFUGEE_NO_DISTRESS_text">[ Refugee ]

Your sensors have picked up a refugee ship drifting through the system, no doubt one of many fleeing the Rebel advance. It doesn't appear to have detected you... or else it is trying to avoid notice.</text>

<text name="event_PIRATE_STATION_CROPS_text">[ Remote settlement ]

Scans show a remote settlement being blockaded by a pirate ship. The ship hastily messages you, "Stay out of this, or you'll be next!...Concentrate fire on..."</text>

<text name="text_BOSS_REPAIR_STATION_1">[ Repair station in Last Stand ]

There is a a mobile ship construction platform stationed at this beacon. After a brief exchange they give you clearance to receive emergency repairs and military supplies.</text>

<text name="text_BOSS_REPAIR_STATION_2">[ Repair station in Last Stand ]

An Engi civilian ship-yard has been converted into a military refueling station. They offer you the chance to patch up your ship and refresh some supplies.</text>

<text name="text_BOSS_REPAIR_STATION_3">[ Repair station in Last Stand ]

Chatter on the comm suggests the nearby Federation base is outfitted with a repair station. When you forward your mission priority they quickly help repair your ship and give you some supplies.</text>

<text name="text_BOSS_REPAIR_STATION_4">[ Repair station in Last Stand ]

A forward construction station is in the process of repairing damaged warships. Your command codes convince them to do a quick patch job on your ship.</text>

<text name="text_BOSS_REPAIR_STATION_5">[ Repair station in Last Stand ]

A trade station was abandoned nearby. Some Federation engineers repurposed their shipyard to perform military repairs. They offer to help fix your ship.</text>

<text name="event_REPAIR_STATION_text">[ Repair station ]

You see a small station fitted with hundreds of Repair drones. You receive an automated message, "We don't know who you are and we don't care, but this is the right place for some ship repair!"</text>

<text name="event_STATION_SICK_text">[ Research station with no response ]

You arrive to find a small research station putting out a distress signal. There is no response to your hails.</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_SLUG_ARGUMENT_text">[ Rock and Slug standoff ]

You find a Slug Cruiser and Rock ship at a standoff, both with weapons armed and ready to fight. You could intervene before this gets out of hand.</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_ATHIEST_text">[ Rock atheists ]

You encounter a small craft with minimal propulsion; its Rock crew-member explains that the Rock home-world is run on lies and propaganda that keep the populace in check, and that they want no part of it.</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_QUEST_MARRIAGE_START_text">[ Rock bride ]

A Rock captain hails you: "It is improper of me to contact off-worlders, but this is an emergency. We were on our way to deliver our passenger to her new husband - the Grand Basilisk of Numa V - when our engines broke down. Will you take possession of her and make haste to Numa V?"</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_FIGHT_ASTEROID_1">[ Rock fight in asteroid field ]

A Rock mining vessel is harvesting the mineral-rich asteroids in this locality, and their scouts take your presence to be a transgression. Battle stations!</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_FIGHT_ASTEROID_2">[ Rock fight in asteroid field ]

A rookie Rock cargo ship has taken its orders too literally and took the most direct route to their destination... right through an asteroid field. They're confused and fire wildly as you jump in.</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_FIGHT_ASTEROID_3">[ Rock fight in asteroid field ]

The captain of a Rock freighter lost in the asteroid field hails you: "Our co-ordinates led us here, but only death greets us. What must be must be. Death to all." You power up the battle systems and wonder how long they've been stuck here.</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_ZOLTAN_ROCK_text">[ Rock fight in nebula ]

This nebula turns out to be the hiding place of a terrified rock crew taking refuge from the Zoltan border police. They don't seem prepared to risk your leaving with their co-ordinates, and open fire!</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_BOARDERS_ASTEROID_1">[ Rock fight with boarders in asteroid field ]

You arrive in an asteroid field and immediately begin evasive maneuvers when a loud clunk reverberates through the ship. At first you think the hull has been hit, but the noise came from some Rock intruders teleporting aboard the ship!</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_BOARDERS_ASTEROID_2">[ Rock fight with boarders in asteroid field ]

Your shields are being taxed as they deflect the debris from an asteroid field. As you weave your way between the rocks, you happen upon a Rock pirate stronghold. You register teleport signatures and hear shouts aboard the ship.</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_BOARDERS_SHIP_1">[ Rock fight with boarders ]

You passively scan a small Rock station that is next to the beacon. However they must not have appreciated your curiosity. A Rock ship pulls away from the station and you register an incoming teleporter signal as well!</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_BOARDERS_SHIP_2">[ Rock fight with boarders ]

You find a Rock ship docked with a damaged Mantis fighter. Before you have a chance to hail them, the ship moves in to attack you and you register teleporter symbols from the disabled ship. They're using Mantis tech to board you!</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_SHIP_1">[ Rock fight ]

You encounter a Rock vessel and attempt to open trading frequencies, but they take it as an act of cultural transgression and open fire.</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_SHIP_2">[ Rock fight ]

You jump into the middle of a Rock excavation project on a nearby moon. Unimpressed with your intrusion they move to defend themselves!</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_SHIP_3">[ Rock fight ]

You intercept chatter from an approaching Rock ship: "Weapons, moving in to engage, arm the tubes." There is no talking to these guys.</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_SHIP_4">[ Rock fight ]

As you jump in, a vast figure appears on the view-screen. The Rock captain rubs the green, moss-like appendage on his chin and then orders his crew to open fire.</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_SHIP_5">[ Rock fight ]

It looks quiet, but you realize your computer is being scanned. A hidden Rock vessel hails you: "Why do you fill your computer with lies?! These are not the holy words!" Before you can interject they open fire.</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_SHIP_6">[ Rock fight ]

You notice a Rock ship performing combat exercises. However, they quickly change their course to engage your ship. They apparently treat unregistered alien ships as handy target practice.</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_SHIP_7">[ Rock fight ]

A loud 'thud' resounds through the ship after jump completion - you've just shunted a Rock fighter and he's already preparing to fire!</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_SHIP_8">[ Rock fight ]

You're intercepted by a Rock salvage operation. They don't seem to mind that you're still on board while they junk your ship.</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_STARSHIP_MINE_text">[ Rock live mine ]

The burnt out hull of a Rock mine layer drifts by. Behind the wreck drifts a live mine; an automated drone that drills into ships' hulls before exploding. It locks onto your ship's signature and heads your way!</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_NURSERY_text">[ Rock nursery ]

Fluctuating life-signs are reported near the surface of a hazy, pock-marked moon in the vicinity. It seems this is a Rock nursery where the young are 'acclimatized' to their religion - only there's been some kind of coup and the students are running amok!</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_PIRATE_ASTEROID_1">[ Rock pirates fight in asteroid field ]

Minute fissures in the shields spark and crackle as the ship jumps into the wake of a huge asteroid. More asteroids follow, as does a lost and aggressive Rock pirate ship.</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_PIRATE_ASTEROID_2">[ Rock pirates fight in asteroid field ]

You exit the jump surrounded by dirt and rocks. Before long a blast is deflected by your shield, but that was no asteroid... Incoming pirate!</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_PIRATE_SUN_1">[ Rock pirates fight near sun ]

Unusual solar activity in this region means you need to get out, quick. The Rock pirate nearby apparently thinks otherwise as they move to attack your ship.</text>

<text name="text_ROCK_PIRATE_SUN_2">[ Rock pirates fight near sun ]

A Rock ship is silhouetted against a sun in supernova. They hail: "Even out here you follow us! We only wish to be left alone!" Out of panic or anger, they charge their weapons.</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_QUEST_MARRIAGE_text">[ Numa V ]

A vast tunnel network near the surface of Numa V indicates an advanced Rock civilization. This must be where you were asked to deliver the passenger.</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_ROCK_RACIST_text">[ Rock ship in plasma storm ]

A Rock armoured transport nearby looks to have lost its bearings, but when you hail they grow suspicious: "Whatever life-form you are, we find you repugnant. We seek no aid. Leave. Now."</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_UNLOCK1_text">[ Rock cruiser unlock, step 1 ]

You are immediately messaged by an imposing looking Rock war vessel, "You're the ship off to 'save the Federation,' aren't you? And you expect to survive with that hunk of junk?"</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_UNLOCK2_text">[ Rock cruiser unlock, step 2 ]

You arrive at the coordinates given and find yourself dangerously close to an M-class star! The other ship messages you, "Let's see how long your puny ship can handle this heat! Prepare for a challenge!"</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_UNLOCK3_text">[ Rock cruiser unlock, step 3 ]

You arrive at a massive Rockman shipyard and notice the ship that had just tried to kill you is docked and already being repaired. "Well fought! I must say I did not expect you to survive."</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_ZOLTAN_HELP_text">[ Rock/Zoltan intervention ]

It seems a Zoltan ship came here to liberate a Rock settlement from their 'oppressive belief system', and that the settlement did not appreciate it - long-range scanners suggest the Zoltan and their pursuers will be here at any moment!</text>

<text name="event_SECRET_WORD_ABADOTH_text">[ Secret word: ABADOTH ]

You have arrived at the coordinates given to you by the dead crewman you attempted to save. There doesn't seem to be anything here - no planets, no vessels, and no clue as to what he meant by sending you here.</text>

<text name="event_SELL_DRONES_STATION_text">[ Sell drone parts for scrap ]

You see a civilian space station with heavy damage. You receive a message, "We've been hit hard by the war. We need more drone parts to speed up our repairs. We'll buy some from you if you have extra."</text>

<text name="event_SELL_MISSILES_STATION_text">[ Sell missiles for scrap ]

There is a black market hub here. You receive a message, "These are dangerous times. If you have extra military-grade explosives, we'll gladly pay you for them."</text>

<text name="event_MERCENARY_WORK_START_text">[ Settlement mercenary work ]

You are immediately contacted by a settlement, "Hello, travelers. Your ship seems to be outfitted for combat...care to take up a bit of mercenary work?"</text>

<text name="event_STRANDED_BEACON_text">[ Single life form on moon ]

It appears the distress beacon is coming from the surface of a nearby moon. Your sensors are picking up a single life form.</text>

<text name="event_FRIENDLY_SLAVER_text">[ Slaver (friendly) ]

You recognize the ship as a well-known slave trader. He hails you and offers you "laborers" for cheap.</text>

<text name="event_PIRATE_SLAVER_text">[ Slaver (hostile) ]

An especially well-armed pirate ship approaches you. "Hand over one of your crew-members and the rest of you can go free unharmed."</text>

<text name="event_SLUG_DISTRESS_RESCUE_text">[ Slocknog ]

You detect life signs on a nearby moon - a lone Slug marooned on its surface. "Ah, a sssentient ssspecies, after all this time. I am Slocknog, a wandering hero ssseeking adventure. You may hire me for a ssmall sssum."</text>

<text name="event_ROCK_SLUG_ARGUMENT_NEBULA_text">[ Slug and Rock standoff in nebula ]

You detect multiple ships running at maximum power nearby, but you can't see anything through this thick nebula.</text>

<text name="event_QUEST_SLUG_PIRATE_TRAP_text">[ Slug comm tapping ]

You arrive to the sight of two Slug ships in communication range. They don't see you.</text>

<text name="event_SLUG_DISTRESS_PILOTING_text">[ Slug allegiance demand ]

The distress signal originates from a tampered jump beacon. A Slug vessel jumps in and announces he has hacked your engines system. "Of course if you, as one of the few remaining ships in the Federation, swear allegiance to the Slug Empire you will be free to go."</text>

<text name="event_SLUG_DRINK_text">[ Slug drink ]

A Slug captain hails and invites himself aboard your ship to present a flask of something slimy. "Now, most gracioussss captain, you must join me please in a drink to our alliance!"</text>

<text name="text_STORM_SLUG_FIGHT_1">[ Slug fight in plasma storm ]

The ion storm here threatens to deactivate your core systems, a fact made all the worse for the largely unaffected Slug ships circling like space-vultures.</text>

<text name="text_STORM_SLUG_FIGHT_2">[ Slug fight in plasma storm ]

The Slug ship that descends into view as you enter the ion storm must have sensed your distress - defensive action!</text>

<text name="text_STORM_SLUG_FIGHT_3">[ Slug fight in plasma storm ]

You arrive in the middle of an ion storm. Slugs generally avoid these storms but you find one waiting in ambush. Prepare for a fight!</text>

<text name="text_STORM_SLUG_FIGHT_4">[ Slug fight in plasma storm ]

You find yourself stuck in the middle of an ion storm with a Slug ship just a short distance away, refusing all hails. You cautiously try to slip further into the clouds, but they turn suddenly to attack!</text>

<text name="event_SLUG_FIGHT_text">[ Slug fight ]

It's rare for the Slugs to stay exposed in open space for long periods - the ship here may be lost, or just passing through, but either way he moves in to attack!</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_SLUG_CHOOSE_DEATH_text">[ Slug hacker (choice) ]

You are immediately hailed by a dangerous looking ship guarding a station. "I'm feeling generouss today. I shall allow you to choose your own death. Which do you like leasst: shields, oxygen, or weaponsss?"</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_SLUG_DOORS_text">[ Slug hacker (doors) ]

There are few more vicious beasts in the galaxy than a Slug with his back to the wall. The faltering ship armed with fire-weapons uses a remote hacking tool to try and disable your door system - they're going to burn you out!</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_SLUG_MEDBAY_text">[ Slug hacker (medical) ]

A Slug ship hails you: "We've detected some worrying radiation coming from your medical unit, perhaps you should take a look?" As he signs off, your system shuts off and their crew teleports aboard from a nearby station. They don't look like engineers.</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_SLUG_OXYGEN_text">[ Slug hacker (oxygen) ]

The Slugs here use a tactic you hoped you'd never see: they use a remote hacking satellite to sabotage your oxygen production system and then charge fire-weapons - you're going to suffocate!</text>

<text name="event_SLUG_DISTRESS_QUESTION_text">[ Slug moons question ]

You arrive near the distress beacon's signal.</text>

<text name="event_SLUG_DISTRESS_TRICK_text">[ Slug oxygen malfunction ]

You find a Slug vessel broadcasting the distress signal and contact them. "Ah, yesss, we are having problems with our oxygen generation unit. Perhaps your crew can assist in repairsss?"</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_SLUG_HULLFIX_text">[ Slug repair station ]

You arrive to find a small Slug repair station. "Greetingsss traveller! Care for a fix up? We could eassily patch up ssome of that damage."</text>

<text name="event_SLUG_DISTRESS_ROCK_text">[ Slug ship boarding Rock ship ]

You arrive to find a Slug ship in the middle of boarding a disabled Rock freighter.</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_SLUG_FAKE_STORE_text">[ Slug store ship ]

A Slug transport ship is stationed near the beacon with a military escort ship. They message you, "We have been waiting for a customer for agesss. Care to see our waresss?"</text>

<text name="event_SLUG_SURRENDER_text">[ Slug surrender ]

"You have besssted us! Will you accept what is in our storeesss in exchange for our livess?"</text>

<text name="event_SLUG_UNLOCK_1_text">[ Slug unlock - the construction platform ]

You arrive to discover an impressive cruiser being worked on by a few smaller ships and guarded by an assault ship. The mobile construction platform is slowly slipping into the clouds. You have not yet been noticed.</text>

<text name="event_SLUG_UNLOCK_SURRENDER_text">[ Slug unlock surrender ]

"You have besssted us! Will you accept what is in our storeesss in exchange for our livess?"</text>

<text name="event_QUEST_CONSTRUCTIONYARD_text">[ Space station under construction ]

You come across a space station under construction. You receive a message from their command tower, "Greetings. We recently lost contact with a cargo ship that was set to deliver more construction materials. Could you help us figure out what happened to them?"</text>

<text name="event_STALEMATE_SURRENDER_text">[ Stalemate surrender ]

The ship suddenly disables their weapons. There's no explanation and they don't respond to hails. It seems during the battle they lost some fuel cells from their storage. You quickly collect it and leave.</text>

<text name="event_START_BEACON_CRYSTAL_text">[ Start beacon (Crystal) ]

You arrive in a sector not listed in any star charts. Strange crystalline ships dot the horizon. Your companion speaks, "Here we are, my home sector. It has been a long time since others have set foot here, I wonder how you will be received."</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_ENGI_1">[ Start beacon (Engi) ]

You have arrived in Engi space. The Mantis have been threatening the Engi core worlds, but you should be able to stock up for your journey.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_ENGI_2">[ Start beacon (Engi) ]

You have arrived in Engi space. The fall of the Federation has brought tough times for these robotic lifeforms, but they're usually willing to help.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_LANIUS_1">[ Start beacon (Lanius) ]

This sector has been largely abandoned since a series of battles decimated the local population. An unusual alien race is reportedly scavenging in the area. You'd best be on guard.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_LANIUS_2">[ Start beacon (Lanius) ]

This sector was the site of many major battles between the Federation and Rebel fleets. Strangely, there's very little evidence of those battles remaining...</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_LANIUS_3">[ Start beacon (Lanius) ]

There have been a number of reports of advanced ships salvaging the wrecks and abandoned mining facilities in this sector. Could it be that the Lanius have resurfaced?</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_LANIUS_4">[ Start beacon (Lanius) ]

The war tore through this civilian sector, and just recently even the few life signs that remained have begun blinking out. Rumours suggest the Lanius are responsible.</text>

<text name="event_START_BEACON_MANTIS_text">[ Start beacon (Mantis) ]

You've entered a poorly charted area of space that's known to be home to the Mantis. Ensure your hull plating is up to scratch and that you have enough fuel in the tank to make it through.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_NEBULA_1">[ Start beacon (nebula) ]

This nebula must have been an important hub at one point; placing all of these jump beacons would be no easy task. However, now it's hardly navigable.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_NEBULA_2">[ Start beacon (nebula) ]

Nebulas were always dangerous places. Many electronics fail in these clouds. You will have to tread lightly.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_NEBULA_3">[ Start beacon (nebula) ]

You've entered a sector thick with nebulas. You'll have to navigate on instinct.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_NEBULA_4">[ Start beacon (nebula) ]

You've entered a nebula-rich sector. You may put a few light years on the fleet, but that's only useful if you make it out the other side.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_NEBULA_5">[ Start beacon (nebula) ]

Thanks to the high nebula density of this sector very little of it has been charted, and rumours of what lurks in the depths abound.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_NEBULA_6">[ Start beacon (nebula) ]

The gases that make up the nebulas in this sector threaten to impair your systems; but you have to press on.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_PIRATE_1">[ Start beacon (Pirate) ]

A few years ago this region was bustling with trade activity. Now it is overrun with bandits and marauders. You should tread lightly here.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_PIRATE_2">[ Start beacon (Pirate) ]

This somewhat isolated region was thrown into chaos at the start of the rebellion. Even in peacetime it was always beset by pirates but now it houses a center of operations for countless pirate fleets.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_PIRATE_3">[ Start beacon (Pirate) ]

If the reports are true, this area has been under the control of pirates for quite some time. Some traders still attempt to trade with the few settlements that remain, but they do so at great risk.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_PIRATE_4">[ Start beacon (Pirate) ]

A few Federation-friendly planets still exist in this sector, but they are constantly under attack by pirate raids. This is a dangerous sector, so be careful.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_REBEL_1">[ Start beacon (Rebel) ]

This sector was bustling with activity just a few years ago. Now, more than half of the jump beacons have been destroyed, many settlements have been abandoned and the Rebels patrol constantly.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_REBEL_2">[ Start beacon (Rebel) ]

This sector was hit hard by the rebellion. The many alien settlements and stations located here are now watched over by almost an equal number of Rebel bases, heavy-handedly 'keeping the peace'.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_REBEL_3">[ Start beacon (Rebel) ]

Once the Federation forces were scattered, the Rebels came down hard on the locals here. Between the 'tax collectors' and military bases, the Rebel presence in this sector is high.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_REBEL_4">[ Start beacon (Rebel) ]

At one point this was one of the most commonly traveled sectors. Knowing that, the Rebels have stationed a number of fleets here. Be careful.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_REBEL_5">[ Start beacon (Rebel) ]

You will have to be very cautious in this sector. The Rebels have full control and are no doubt looking for you.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_ROCK_1">[ Start beacon (Rock) ]

The Rock people have a particularly aggressive stance toward alien races trespassing in their space. You should tread carefully here.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_ROCK_2">[ Start beacon (Rock) ]

The Rock people are a powerful and proud race. It is not unheard of to have a peaceful journey through their lands, but don't count on it.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_SLUG_1">[ Start beacon (Slug) ]

The only thing that can render a nebula more dangerous is if it's also home to the Slugs. This particular nebula is just that.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_SLUG_2">[ Start beacon (Slug) ]

This nebula is home to the telepathic Slugs. They'd sell their own slime for a crate of scrap, but they much prefer to just take it.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_SLUG_3">[ Start beacon (Slug) ]

You're told the Slug home world is somewhere in this nebula. You can't see them, but you know they're watching.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_SLUG_4">[ Start beacon (Slug) ]

The Slugs that live in this nebula field are a leisure-centered civilization. Everything in Slug life is done in the pursuit of more currency and more time in which to spend it on extravagant ventures. This, inevitably, leads to much treachery in open space.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_SLUG_5">[ Start beacon (Slug) ]

The Slugs developed on an ocean planet where the ability to telepathically sense another organism was more important than sight. Today they use this ability to navigate unfettered the depths of the nebulas they inhabit.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_ZOLTAN_1">[ Start beacon (Zoltan) ]

You've entered Zoltan territory. This species is not renowned for giving anything for nothing, but you can always be assured a fair hearing.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_ZOLTAN_2">[ Start beacon (Zoltan) ]

The Zoltan patrol their borders but let you pass when you ID as Federation. Let's hope they won't be so courteous to the Rebels.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_ZOLTAN_3">[ Start beacon (Zoltan) ]

You arrive in Zoltan space. From what you have heard they anticipated the coming war and made preparations to hold their borders.</text>

<text name="text_START_BEACON_ZOLTAN_4">[ Start beacon (Zoltan) ]

You're far from Federation home space here in Zoltan territory, and it's not clear whether the authorities will have any goodwill remaining. Still, you have to push forward.</text>

<text name="event_START_BEACON_text">[ Start beacon ]

Welcome to a new sector! Get to the exit beacon and jump to the next sector before the pursuing Rebels catch you!</text>

<text name="event_START_DEMO_text">[ Start demo ]

Welcome to the Federation training simulation! You're about to be sent on a very dangerous mission carrying data vital to the Federation fleet. We've put this simulator together to give you an idea of what to expect on the actual journey. Explore the sector, gather supplies, but get to the exit before the simulated Rebel fleet catches up!</text>

<text name="event_START_GAME_text">[ Start game ]

The data you carry is vital to the remaining Federation fleet. You'll need supplies for the journey, so make sure to explore each sector before moving on to the next. But get to the exit before the pursuing Rebel fleet can catch up!</text>

<text name="text_STORE_ENGI_1">[ Store (Engi) ]

The Engi can do remarkable things with just a pile of scrap. The Engi hive at this beacon are selling equipment for just that.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_ENGI_2">[ Store (Engi) ]

A message arrives: "Your scrap, ours. Our weapons for you." You're about to raise the shields when you realize it's just an Engi trader looking for a trade.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_ENGI_3">[ Store (Engi) ]

An Engi ship hails: "Engine upgrade necessary for travel home. Sale of equipment necessary for engine upgrade."</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_STORE_SLUG_1">[ Store in nebula (Slug) ]

A huge Slug teleports from nowhere onto the bridge! Before you can open fire, he's spread his wares across the helm and is brandishing things at you.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_STORE_SLUG_2">[ Store in nebula (Slug) ]

You cautiously approach a Slug colony on a huge asteroid. It's a brave person who sets foot on a Slug planet - it can take weeks to get the mucus out of your clothes - but there's business to be done.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_STORE_1">[ Store in nebula (Uncharted) ]

Some brave entrepreneurs set up a station here to extract elements from the nebula. There seems to be a public shipyard and rest stop here as well.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_STORE_2">[ Store in nebula (Uncharted) ]

Seeing a trade depot set up near the beacon implies there is an alien settlement on some nearby rock. You decide to check out their wares.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_STORE_3">[ Store in nebula (Uncharted) ]

The centre of a hydrogen cloud doesn't seem like a very usual place for a store, but the Engi aren't a usual species. Wouldn't hurt to take a look.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_STORE_4">[ Store in nebula (Uncharted) ]

An Engi cargo vessel hails: "Propose mutually beneficial exchange of properties." That smells like a bargain.</text>

<text name="text_NEBULA_STORE_5">[ Store in nebula (Uncharted) ]

You discover a cluster of Federation refugee ships taking shelter in the folds of the nebula. "I'm sorry we've got nothing to give you, but we need scrap to keep the engines running." You sense they'll strike a trade.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_LANIUS_1">[ Store (Lanius) ]

A large transport ship undergoing maintenance hails you. "Greetings, friend. We're getting out of this sector as soon as this Coolant Shaft is fixed and I suggest you do the same. I half expect those damn metal freaks to come and try to melt down our ship at any moment. We're trying to offload some inventory - interested in buying something?"</text>

<text name="text_STORE_LANIUS_2">[ Store (Lanius) ]

You arrive to discover a number of Lanius ships docked at what appears to be a station. You hasten to leave but are relieved when they message you in your language. "Buy? Sell? Traders." Apparently some merchants emigrated with the scavengers.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_LANIUS_3">[ Store (Lanius) ]

A trading depot is set up near the beacon. A surprising number of military ships guard the station. You pick up an advertisement on a wide band channel, "Ship parts, repairs, refueling, souvenirs - we got it all. Check out the only store not afraid of scavengers this side of Omacron 6."</text>

<text name="text_STORE_LANIUS_4">[ Store (Lanius) ]

You arrive at an empty space station, no doubt abandoned due to the Lanius threat. Life signatures are detected at the ship depot and you spot a few crude signs stating "Everything Must Go!"</text>

<text name="text_STORE_LANIUS_5">[ Store (Lanius) ]

This beacon is bustling with activity. It looks like some merchants decided to capitalize on the fact that dozens of refugee ships are using this location to recharge their FTL drives. You browse their wares.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_LANIUS_6">[ Store (Lanius) ]

You receive a message from a nearby station, "The end is upon us! The metal demons have come to absorb your very being! But it's not too late to prepare for the worst!" It appears that was an advertisement for a space dock. You scan their products.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_MANTIS_1">[ Store (Mantis) ]

Upon arriving at the beacon, you're hailed by a well-spoken Mantis, "Hail, traveler. These are dangerous times. Perhaps you find yourself in need of our services?" He appears to be a trader.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_MANTIS_2">[ Store (Mantis) ]

Uncertain about what you'll discover at this beacon, you scan the surroundings. You detect several warnings on wide-band channels discouraging any violence in protected trade-space. Perhaps you can find some wares nearby.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_MANTIS_3">[ Store (Mantis) ]

Merchants are not highly respected among the Mantis race, so few undertake the profession. You're mildly surprised to receive an advertisement from a nearby space dock. You decide to see what they have to offer.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_MANTIS_4">[ Store (Mantis) ]

Identifying a Mantis trading post ahead, you signal them so that your approach won't be taken as a threat. The leader hails you: "You have scrap? Quickly, come dock before the warriors see you."</text>

<text name="text_STORE_MANTIS_5">[ Store (Mantis) ]

A struggling Mantis cargo ship headed for the node raises what's left of shields as you jump in. You power up your weapons as a show of force, and they reluctantly agree to offload some of their cargo to you - for a price.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_MANTIS_6">[ Store (Mantis) ]

The Rebels are already here! The crew braces for impact, but none comes. The sensors report the unmanned rebel supply ship is malfunctioning and is stuck in vending mode - for a little scrap you can take your pick.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_PIRATE_1">[ Store (Pirate) ]

A few small ships are visible on the vidscreen, and you almost activate weapons targeting. However, sensors indicate they are simply honest merchants. The pirates must be making you jumpy. You message them asking about their wares.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_PIRATE_2">[ Store (Pirate) ]

You detect a hub of activity nearby. A large corporation has set up a trade depot and has a number of well armed ships patrolling. This appears to be a relatively safe place to get repairs.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_PIRATE_3">[ Store (Pirate) ]

You receive a wide-band automated message, "Welcome to our humble trade depot and shipyard! All are welcome, but try any funny business and our 152 automated turret satellites will tear your ship to shreds!"</text>

<text name="text_STORE_PIRATE_4">[ Store (Pirate) ]

A well armed transport ship and a squadron of fighters are in orbit nearby. You are wary of their trustworthiness but beggars can't be choosers.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_REBEL_1">[ Store (Rebel) ]

You discover a re-supply station used by Rebels and civilians alike. You transmit your fake ship identification and for once, they don't seem to recognize your ship. You try to assume the air of a local as you prepare to dock.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_REBEL_2">[ Store (Rebel) ]

You arrive at a small space station that is putting out wide-band broadcasts on black-market channels. You doubt they would turn away any business, regardless of allegiances.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_REBEL_3">[ Store (Rebel) ]

You receive generic advertisements from a nearby public ship-yard. It seems they are willing to work on any ship, not only those of Rebel hue.</text>

<text name="event_STORE_RESCUE_text">[ Store rescue ]

Once you arrive at this populated region, you immediately pick up a distress signal. A small shuttle is asking anyone who'll listen for help protecting their family from a Rebel ship. Unsurprisingly, no one has yet responded to their request.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_ROCK_1">[ Store (Rock) ]

You cross paths with a Rock ship returning from a rare diplomatic mission. Equally surprising, the captain responds to your hails and agrees to a mutual trade.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_ROCK_2">[ Store (Rock) ]

You come across a Rock trading post. It's rare they deal with outsiders, but they need to sell the last of their stock, and will pay their dues for their transgression when they return home.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_ROCK_3">[ Store (Rock) ]

With the local Rock settlements so unwilling to trade with other life forms, an opportunistic Mantis crew has postponed its piracy activities and set up shop to catch any passing trade.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_ROCK_4">[ Store (Rock) ]

The Rock tolerate few aliens in their space, but even they seem to respect the wisdom of the Zoltan - a few of them have established a trading post in the husk of an abandoned capital ship.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_ROCK_5">[ Store (Rock) ]

You receive a hail on Federation frequencies: "You're Federation?! We- we weren't sure we'd ever see a friendly face again. There's little business here, perhaps you'd like to trade?"</text>

<text name="text_STORE_ZOLTAN_1">[ Store (Zoltan) ]

The Zoltan are fascinated by other species, and have set up something of an alien knick-knack shop here. Why not take a look?</text>

<text name="text_STORE_ZOLTAN_2">[ Store (Zoltan) ]

A human ship hails: "My friends! Please, there is nothing I don't have, and there is nothing worth wanting that I can't get. Why not take a look around my shop?"</text>

<text name="text_STORE_ZOLTAN_3">[ Store (Zoltan) ]

A Mantis crew here has hunkered down in the abdomen of a long-dead space-whale - the only way, presumably, for them to operate their black-market trade without detection. Worth a look?</text>

<text name="text_STORE_TEXT_1">[ Store ]

A ship engineer has set up a small shop here.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_TEXT_2">[ Store ]

You find yourself surrounded by a group of mysterious alien vessels. They hail you and apparently have some valuable technology for sale.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_TEXT_3">[ Store ]

A transmission from the nearby planet indicates an outpost below which offers supplies to travelers. You send down an away party to check it out.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_TEXT_4">[ Store ]

The space station here has a traveling merchant who shows you his wares.</text>

<text name="text_STORE_TEXT_5">[ Store ]

There is only one other ship at this beacon, and it is showing heavy damage. You receive a message on your console: "Greetings, traveler. We were crippled by a band of pirates and are now forced to sell our remaining valuable equipment to acquire the necessary supplies to get home."</text>

<text name="event_TERRAFORMING_SCAN_text">[ Terraforming scan ]

You receive a hail from a station orbiting a nearby planet. "Captain, we are Federation Terraforming Team C12 and are in need of assistance. Do you have some time?"</text>

<text name="event_DONOR_BLACK_RAVEN_text">[ The Black Raven ]

As you jump in, you immediately see an impressive Slug pirate ship with "The Black Raven" painted on one side. They hail you, "Greetingsss. I am the dreaded pirate, Captain Nights. You mussst be full of fear, no? You have heard of me... no?"</text>

<text name="event_ENGI_VIRUS_text">[ The Engi virus ]

The Engi are awaiting you at the beacon, with their weapons on-line! They explain a computer virus that is wanted for hostile acts against the Engi (multiple counts of binary scrambling, nano-dissolution, and variable interference) is aboard your vessel.</text>

<text name="text_MERCENARY_1">[ The mercenary ]

You find a mercenary for hire at this Beacon. Their unique skills can sometimes prove to be useful.</text>

<text name="text_MERCENARY_2">[ The mercenary ]

A mercenary hails you: "Greetings, friend! We've heard tell of your quest and are here to offer our valuable services."</text>

<text name="text_MERCENARY_3">[ The mercenary ]

There's a ship with pirate markings orbiting the nearby planet. You receive his hail: "Anything is possible, for the right price."</text>

<text name="text_MERCENARY_4">[ The mercenary ]

The captain of this ship claims he can provide "services" as long as you've got the scrap.</text>

<text name="text_MERCENARY_5">[ The mercenary ]

Mercenaries are swarming the galaxy now, knowing that their less-than-legal services are in demand during this period of unrest. One is waiting at this beacon and hails you.</text>

<text name="text_MERCENARY_6">[ The mercenary ]

A ship hails you: "Good sir! It seems you're having some troubles with the Rebels. I'd like to help you, but I can't afford the upkeep required on this hunk of junk I'm flying... maybe we can come to an arrangement?"</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FOR_DRONE_1">[ Trade fuel for drone parts ]

A nearby space station hails you. "Greetings! Your arrival is most fortuitous. We recently came across some extra drones. If you have some fuel, perhaps we can make a deal?"</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FOR_DRONE_2">[ Trade fuel for drone parts ]

A strange vessel approaches. A digital message appears on your view-screen: "This is an automated merchant. Refill this vessel with fuel and it will supply you with drones."</text>

<text name="text_FUEL_FOR_DRONE_3">[ Trade fuel for drone parts ]

You arrive in the sector and are greeted by a science vessel waiting by the beacon. They hail you, "We find ourselves low on fuel and have a proposition."</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_TRADER_text">[ Trade resources in nebula ]

It's hard to see why, but this beacon is apparently a tourist destination. One of the ships at the small station is offering a deal.</text>

<text name="text_TRADER_CIV_1">[ Trade resources ]

You arrive at a quiet spaceport and are immediately hailed by another ship at port with a "once in a lifetime deal!"</text>

<text name="text_TRADER_CIV_2">[ Trade resources ]

You jump into a sector filled with civilian activity. Your scan the various advertisement channels while waiting for your FTL to charge, and are intrigued by a grey-market shipwright.</text>

<text name="text_TRADER_CIV_3">[ Trade resources ]

Your ship is flooded with advertisement transmissions from nearby merchants as soon as you arrive at this beacon. You arbitrarily pick one to examine in detail.</text>

<text name="text_TRADER_CIV_4">[ Trade resources ]

Despite the barren area, a trader has set up shop at this beacon. He presents his offer.</text>

<text name="text_TRADER_CIV_5">[ Trade resources ]

The beacon at first glance seems home to a junk yard. Upon closer inspection, it reveals itself to be a ramshackle market. One trader has a deal that catches your eye.</text>

<text name="text_TRADER_CIV_6">[ Trade resources ]

A pawn broker has set up shop at this obscure beacon. He might be offering something worth looking at.</text>

<text name="text_TRADER_UPGRADES_TEXT_1">[ Trade scrap for upgrades ]

You are immediately hailed by a mobile docking platform upon arrival, "Welcome to Uncle Joe's Fix-it Shop! Need a tuneup? We got you covered!"</text>

<text name="text_TRADER_UPGRADES_TEXT_2">[ Trade scrap for upgrades ]

There are a number of privately owned ship construction platforms in the area. You find one that has a slot open for some immediate work.</text>

<text name="text_TRADER_UPGRADES_TEXT_3">[ Trade scrap for upgrades ]

You pick up an automated message from a nearby space station. There appears to be a local shipwright that can perform emergency work on military ships.</text>

<text name="text_TRADER_UPGRADES_TEXT_4">[ Trade scrap for upgrades ]

You receive a message from a small refugee convoy, "Hail. We'd like to help you on your mission but don't have much to offer. If you have extra metal perhaps we could work on your ship?"</text>

<text name="event_TUTORIAL_START_text">[ Tutorial start ]

Welcome to FTL! You are the captain of a Federation starship on a very important mission.</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_PEACE_QUEST_text">[ Unarmed Zoltan transport ]

An unarmed Zoltan transport vessel is slowly making its way toward the beacon here. They hail: "This is a Zoltan peace envoy. We carry no weapons or shielding and rely on the mercy of others to communicate our message."</text>

<text name="event_DISTRESS_STATION_DISEASE_text">[ Unknown disease on mining colony ]

You locate a nearby human mining colony where an unknown disease has spread virulently. They are setting up a quarantine to contain it but a riot has broken out.</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_BOARDERS_text">[ Zoltan border police ]

There are few more zealous in their customs checks than the Zoltan. A team of border police beam on board. There's just a little confusion over your weapons licences, but things escalate rapidly from heated discussion to gunfire!</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_ASTEROID_text">[ Zoltan fight in asteroid field ]

You arrive in an asteroid field and are greeted by a Zoltan guard, "By attempting to access these closed mining fields, you are in violation of the Natural Mineral Protection Act. Your weaponry will be confiscated for processing." You don't have time for this.</text>

<text name="text_ZOLTAN_FIGHT_1">[ Zoltan fight ]

A Zoltan ship makes contact. "The nature of the day is rotational. The fever is emaciated. The reason is-" They've caught some nasty deep space dementia. Before you can consider finding help for them, they open fire.</text>

<text name="text_ZOLTAN_FIGHT_2">[ Zoltan fight ]

You're surprised when a stationary Zoltan ship opens fire. It appears there are aggressive pugilists even among the 'enlightened'.</text>

<text name="text_ZOLTAN_FIGHT_3">[ Zoltan fight ]

You receive a message, "This area is off limits. Submit your ship to processing." It's only one guard ship in a lonely beacon. You decide to fight your way out.</text>

<text name="text_ZOLTAN_FIGHT_4">[ Zoltan fight ]

You discover a number of Zoltan civilian ships fighting off pirates. Unfortunately one ship mistakes your purpose and moves in to attack! They are refusing all communication; you have no choice but to fight.</text>

<text name="text_ZOLTAN_FIGHT_5">[ Zoltan fight ]

Like many areas in Zoltan space, the residents of this sector prepared well for Galactic war. The military here seem to have given up reasoning with foreigners, preferring instead to attack on sight!</text>

<text name="text_ZOLTAN_FIGHT_6">[ Zoltan fight ]

A Zoltan ship is waiting at this beacon. They request your identification, but radiation from the sun in this system is disrupting your communications. They take your silence for aggression and move in to attack.</text>

<text name="text_ZOLTAN_FIGHT_7">[ Zoltan fight ]

The Zoltan ship patrolling this area hails you: "This area is off limits. Secrecy is vital." They power their weapons.</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_FREE_AUGMENT_text">[ Zoltan free augment ]

A Zoltan academy sits docked just outside the beacon perimeter. They're happy to show you the fruits of their labor, and offer something to take home with you.</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_FREE_MAP_text">[ Zoltan free map ]

The Zoltan stationed near this beacon are happy to receive you. As they give you the formal tour of their ship you spy some local star charts and mentally log the details.</text>

<text name="event_NEBULA_ZOLTAN_EYE_text">[ Zoltan Great Eye ]

Inside this nebula you detect a rogue planet drifting through space, on its surface a huge monolith visible at this distance even to the naked eye. A Zoltan elder hails you from the planet. "Through luck or intent, you have discovered the Great Eye. Look into its depths and receive your just deserts."</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_ODD_MOON_text">[ Zoltan odd moon ]

Something strikes you as odd about a moon in the distance.</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_PEACE_QUEST2_text">[ Zoltan peace quest - the brethren's coordinates ]

You arrive at the location specified by the peace-loving Zoltan, but the only thing nearby is a Rebel ship, closing in fast! "We've found you! You're not getting away this time!"</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_QUEST_PRIMITIVES_text">[ Zoltan quest primitives ]

You arrive at the primitive planet that you heard about at the cantina and are surprised to see a Zoltan ship facing off against a Rebel assault craft.</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_CREW_STUDY_text">[ Zoltan research facility ]

You arrive at a Zoltan research facility. They say they are researching genetic distortion due to stasis sleep and prolonged FTL travel. They ask if your crew has the time to undergo a few scans.</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_LIFERAFT_text">[ Zoltan retake the ship ]

You pick up a Zoltan life raft floating in space. Its inhabitant asks you to retake his ship from the pirates who recently commandeered it. "I'm certain it is clear," he concludes, "that you must not destroy my vessel in the process."</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_RIFT_SUCCESS_text">[ Zoltan rift - victory aftermath ]

When he sees you have emerged victorious, the Zoltan wise man enters a rage. Rifts threaten to tear space apart until, instead, the Zoltan implodes, sending a blast wave of scrap and salvage dragged here from distant worlds in your direction.</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_CREW_SCAN_text">[ Zoltan security checkpoint ]

You arrive at a Zoltan security checkpoint set up in a perimeter around the beacon. "Travelling vessel, you will submit to crew profiling to identify fugitives of the empire."</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_SCIENCE_DOCK_text">[ Zoltan ship asks to dock ]

What appears to be a Zoltan science ship requests permission to dock.</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_DISTRESS_MANTIS_text">[ Zoltan ship follows Mantis ship ]

Your jump interrupts a Zoltan security ship as it follows a Mantis pirate into an asteroid field. They message you, "Your presence here will continue to be tolerated - but please, do not interfere."</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_TRADE_HUB_text">[ Zoltan trade hub ]

You come to a Zoltan trade and supply hub - everything the weary traveler needs, provided they have the right documentation.</text>

<text name="event_ZOLTAN_RIFT_FIGHT_text">[ Zoltan wise man ]

You come to a quiet part of Zoltan space and encounter an ancient Zoltan wise man who has managed to harness the power of a spatial rift, but seems to have been driven completely mad by the power. "Choose your doom," he demands. This is all part of a day's work.</text>
